window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/owner-courses/b163-ee397b031af86a83.json"]={sha256:"ee397b031af86a8372d2fd2cef5a018a4206f3e5192adaa9d824bd02f8bf896f",value:{"id":"b163","title":"高水壓隧道止水灌漿","titleEn":"Water-control grouting in high-pressure tunnels","category":"underground","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"本課以用水頭、壓力損失與滲流證據評估高水壓止水灌漿為主線，從水頭基準與孔隙水壓與泵表讀值與孔段壓力建立系統邊界，再把幾何體積與實際注入量、前後透水比較與水頭連到驗收範圍與長期水路。算例只描述水力關係，不提供現地配方、注入壓力或施作授權。 十單元以可核算的模型和可追溯證據逐步判讀不同失效。","summaryEn":"This course focuses on assess high-head water-control grouting using head, pressure loss and seepage evidence. It begins with Head datum and pore pressure and Pump gauge and interval pressure, links Geometric volume and delivered volume and Before-after permeability and head, and ends with Acceptance coverage and long-term pathways. Examples describe hydraulic relationships, not field recipes, injection pressures or operating authorization. Ten units use reproducible models and traceable evidence to distinguish failure mechanisms.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、開挖、注漿或受限空間作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, excavation, grouting or confined-space permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"ug-water","subcategoryTitle":"地下水與防排水","subcategoryTitleEn":"Groundwater and waterproofing","learningTrack":"underground","learningSubdiscipline":"ug-water","learningTags":["underground","ug-water","water"],"architectureFamily":"water","architectureNodes":[["水頭基準與孔隙水壓","Head datum and pore pressure"],["孔隙壓與有效作用差","Pore pressure and net pressure difference"],["幾何體積與實際注入量","Geometric volume and delivered volume"],["前後透水比較與水頭","Before-after permeability and head"],["驗收範圍與長期水路","Acceptance coverage and long-term pathways"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[0,3]],"diagram":{"type":"water","labels":["水頭基準與孔隙水壓","孔隙壓與有效作用差","幾何體積與實際注入量","前後透水比較與水頭","驗收範圍與長期水路"],"labelsEn":["Head datum and pore pressure","Pore pressure and net pressure difference","Geometric volume and delivered volume","Before-after permeability and head","Acceptance coverage and long-term pathways"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"整合算例所有輸入均為教學假設。首先檢查水頭基準與孔隙水壓：Inputs rho=1000 kg/m3, g=9.81 m/s2, h=80 m; p=rho*g*h=1000*9.81*80=784800 Pa=0.7848 MPa；再獨立檢查泵表讀值與孔段壓力：Inputs conveyed-fluid density=1000 kg/m3, g=9.81 m/s2, downward elevation change=10 m; pInterval=0.90 MPa+0.0981 MPa-0.15 MPa=0.8481 MPa; another grout density requires recalculating the hydrostatic term。水頭由 80 增為 100 m，淡水靜壓由 0.7848 增為 0.981 MPa；泵壓仍須修正高程及沿程損失，不能把差值當成允許提高注壓的指令。 兩個結果不能自動組成完整設計，因為算例只描述水力關係，不提供現地配方、注入壓力或施作授權。 將將地表水準、結構位移和相鄰孔壓放在共同時間軸作為模型以外的驗證證據，並保留原始紀錄與尚待確認的邊界。","textEn":"All inputs in this integrated example are teaching assumptions. First check Head datum and pore pressure: Inputs rho=1000 kg/m3, g=9.81 m/s2, h=80 m; p=rho*g*h=1000*9.81*80=784800 Pa=0.7848 MPa. Independently check Pump gauge and interval pressure: Inputs conveyed-fluid density=1000 kg/m3, g=9.81 m/s2, downward elevation change=10 m; pInterval=0.90 MPa+0.0981 MPa-0.15 MPa=0.8481 MPa; another grout density requires recalculating the hydrostatic term. Increasing freshwater head from 80 to 100 m raises static pressure from 0.7848 to 0.981 MPa; pump readings still require elevation and loss corrections, not an instruction to increase field pressure. The two results are not a complete design because examples describe hydraulic relationships, not field recipes, injection pressures or operating authorization. Use align surface levels, structural movement and neighbouring pore pressures as evidence independent of the calculation, retaining raw records and unverified boundaries.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":14,"enrichmentVersion":14,"stages":[{"id":"b163-v14-s1","title":"地層條件、邊界與工程系統","titleEn":"Ground conditions, boundaries and engineering system","description":"本階段聚焦「水頭基準與孔隙水壓」與「泵表讀值與孔段壓力」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Head datum and pore pressure\" and \"Pump gauge and interval pressure\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b163-v14-01","title":"水頭基準與孔隙水壓：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Head datum and pore pressure: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「水頭基準與孔隙水壓」如何影響高水壓隧道止水灌漿的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Head datum and pore pressure” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Water-control grouting in high-pressure tunnels”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"高水壓首先是水位與量測點高程的關係，埋深不一定等於水頭。承壓含水層可在地表以上形成測壓水位，不同孔段也可能不連通；應把量測位置和基準高程清楚標出，再比較外部水壓與隧道內部條件。 判別這個機制時，應觀察將分段測壓水位、孔口高程及量測深度換到共同基準；若出現混用地表深度與水頭使設計水壓估錯，錯判止水需求，便須重新檢查原先假設的接觸、力或水的傳遞邊界，而不能只調整計算結果。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「水頭基準與孔隙水壓」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"High pressure depends on piezometric level relative to the measurement point, not burial depth alone. Confined levels may exceed ground surface and different intervals may be disconnected. Identify measurement elevations and datums before comparing external water pressure with tunnel conditions. Use the following check to discriminate the mechanism: Reduce interval heads, collar elevations and measurement depths to a common datum. If confusing depth with head misestimates water pressure and water-control demand, revisit the assumed contact, force or water-transfer boundary rather than merely adjusting the calculated result. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Head datum and pore pressure” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：Inputs rho=1000 kg/m3, g=9.81 m/s2, h=80 m; p=rho*g*h=1000*9.81*80=784800 Pa=0.7848 MPa。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: Inputs rho=1000 kg/m3, g=9.81 m/s2, h=80 m; p=rho*g*h=1000*9.81*80=784800 Pa=0.7848 MPa.","failure":"常見誤解：「隧道埋得多深就一定有完全相同的地下水頭」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Tunnel burial depth always equals the groundwater head\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「水頭基準與孔隙水壓」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Head datum and pore pressure”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b163-v14-01-k1","title":"水頭基準與孔隙水壓","titleEn":"Head datum and pore pressure","text":"高水壓首先是水位與量測點高程的關係，埋深不一定等於水頭。承壓含水層可在地表以上形成測壓水位，不同孔段也可能不連通；應把量測位置和基準高程清楚標出，再比較外部水壓與隧道內部條件。","textEn":"High pressure depends on piezometric level relative to the measurement point, not burial depth alone. Confined levels may exceed ground surface and different intervals may be disconnected.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"]},{"id":"b163-v14-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：隧道埋得多深就一定有完全相同的地下水頭 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Tunnel burial depth always equals the groundwater head Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「水頭基準與孔隙水壓」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Head datum and pore pressure\" is correct?","options":["隧道埋得多深就一定有完全相同的地下水頭","高水壓首先是水位與量測點高程的關係，埋深不一定等於水頭。","泵表壓力永遠等於灌漿孔段實際壓力"],"optionsEn":["Tunnel burial depth always equals the groundwater head","High pressure depends on piezometric level relative to the measurement point, not burial depth alone.","Pump-gauge pressure always equals actual pressure in the treated interval"],"answer":1,"explanation":"高水壓首先是水位與量測點高程的關係，埋深不一定等於水頭。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"High pressure depends on piezometric level relative to the measurement point, not burial depth alone. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b163-v14-02","title":"水頭基準與孔隙水壓：定量估算","titleEn":"Head datum and pore pressure: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b163-v14-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「水頭基準與孔隙水壓」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Head datum and pore pressure” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：Inputs rho=1000 kg/m3, g=9.81 m/s2, h=80 m; p=rho*g*h=1000*9.81*80=784800 Pa=0.7848 MPa。算例只描述水力關係，不提供現地配方、注入壓力或施作授權。 此結果僅用來核對量綱及模型敏感度，不是專案設計值、實測紀錄或現場允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: Inputs rho=1000 kg/m3, g=9.81 m/s2, h=80 m; p=rho*g*h=1000*9.81*80=784800 Pa=0.7848 MPa. Examples describe hydraulic relationships, not field recipes, injection pressures or operating authorization. This checks dimensions and model sensitivity; it is neither measured project data nor a design or acceptance value. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將分段測壓水位、孔口高程及量測深度換到共同基準。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Reduce interval heads, collar elevations and measurement depths to a common datum.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b163-v14-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：Inputs rho=1000 kg/m3, g=9.81 m/s2, h=80 m; p=rho*g*h=1000*9.81*80=784800 Pa=0.7848 MPa。算例只描述水力關係，不提供現地配方、注入壓力或施作授權。 此結果僅用來核對量綱及模型敏感度，不是專案設計值、實測紀錄或現場允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Inputs rho=1000 kg/m3, g=9.81 m/s2, h=80 m; p=rho*g*h=1000*9.81*80=784800 Pa=0.7848 MPa. Examples describe hydraulic relationships, not field recipes, injection pressures or operating authorization. This checks dimensions and model sensitivity; it is neither measured project data nor a design or acceptance value.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"]},{"id":"b163-v14-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「水頭基準與孔隙水壓」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Head datum and pore pressure\", which statement holds?","options":["所有裂隙對總漏水的貢獻都大致相同","入口壓力升高就能證明整個處理區都已封閉","原創教學假設：Inputs rho=1000 kg/m3, g=9.81 m/s2, h=80 m; p=rho*g*h=1000*9.81*80=784800 Pa=0.7848 MPa。"],"optionsEn":["Every fracture contributes approximately equally to total leakage","Rising entrance pressure proves the entire treated zone is sealed","Original teaching assumptions: Inputs rho=1000 kg/m3, g=9.81 m/s2, h=80 m; p=rho*g*h=1000*9.81*80=784800 Pa=0.7848 MPa."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：Inputs rho=1000 kg/m3, g=9.81 m/s2, h=80 m; p=rho*g*h=1000*9.81*80=784800 Pa=0.7848 MPa。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Inputs rho=1000 kg/m3, g=9.81 m/s2, h=80 m; p=rho*g*h=1000*9.81*80=784800 Pa=0.7848 MPa. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b163-v14-03","title":"水頭基準與孔隙水壓：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Head datum and pore pressure: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b163-v14-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「水頭基準與孔隙水壓」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Head datum and pore pressure” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將分段測壓水位、孔口高程及量測深度換到共同基準。量測須保存位置、時間及基準，讓同條件的重複結果可比較；並特別檢查「混用地表深度與水頭使設計水壓估錯，錯判止水需求」是否能由這組資料區分。儀器校核與誤差估計應先於判讀，由負責技師核定該項試驗的允收和停留點。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Reduce interval heads, collar elevations and measurement depths to a common datum. Retain position, time and datums for comparable repeats, specifically distinguishing this scenario: Confusing depth with head misestimates water pressure and water-control demand. Instrument checks and uncertainty estimates precede interpretation; the responsible engineer sets acceptance and hold points for this test. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將將分段測壓水位、孔口高程及量測深度換到共同基準列為該構件的交接證據，連結到施工位置、材料批次及判讀版本。若發現混用地表深度與水頭使設計水壓估錯，錯判止水需求，先保留原始紀錄並由負責技師確認處置，不能以本課算例替代核定作業計畫。","observationEn":"Site practice: Apply the following check at handover: Reduce interval heads, collar elevations and measurement depths to a common datum. Link results to location, material batch and interpretation version. If confusing depth with head misestimates water pressure and water-control demand, retain original records and obtain the responsible engineer's disposition; this example does not replace an approved work plan.","failure":"注意干擾：混用地表深度與水頭使設計水壓估錯，錯判止水需求。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Confusing depth with head misestimates water pressure and water-control demand. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b163-v14-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將分段測壓水位、孔口高程及量測深度換到共同基準。量測須保存位置、時間及基準，讓同條件的重複結果可比較；並特別檢查「混用地表深度與水頭使設計水壓估錯，錯判止水需求」是否能由這組資料區分。儀器校核與誤差估計應先於判讀，由負責技師核定該項試驗的允收和停留點。","textEn":"Reduce interval heads, collar elevations and measurement depths to a common datum. Retain position, time and datums for comparable repeats, specifically distinguishing this scenario: Confusing depth with head misestimates water pressure and water-control demand. Instrument checks and uncertainty estimates precede interpretation; the responsible engineer sets acceptance and hold points for this test.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"]},{"id":"b163-v14-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將將分段測壓水位、孔口高程及量測深度換到共同基準列為該構件的交接證據，連結到施工位置、材料批次及判讀版本。若發現混用地表深度與水頭使設計水壓估錯，錯判止水需求，先保留原始紀錄並由負責技師確認處置，不能以本課算例替代核定作業計畫。","textEn":"Apply the following check at handover: Reduce interval heads, collar elevations and measurement depths to a common datum. Link results to location, material batch and interpretation version. If confusing depth with head misestimates water pressure and water-control demand, retain original records and obtain the responsible engineer's disposition; this example does not replace an approved work plan.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「水頭基準與孔隙水壓」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Head datum and pore pressure\"?","options":["將分段測壓水位、孔口高程及量測深度換到共同基準。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、開挖序列與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","孔口周圍沒變形就能證明所有遠端地層都沒反應"],"optionsEn":["Reduce interval heads, collar elevations and measurement depths to a common datum.","Temperature, water head, excavation sequence and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","No movement near the collar proves all distant ground remains unaffected"],"answer":0,"explanation":"將分段測壓水位、孔口高程及量測深度換到共同基準。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Reduce interval heads, collar elevations and measurement depths to a common datum. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b163-v14-04","title":"水頭基準與孔隙水壓：失效診斷","titleEn":"Head datum and pore pressure: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b163-v14-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「水頭基準與孔隙水壓」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Head datum and pore pressure” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"混用地表深度與水頭使設計水壓估錯，錯判止水需求。相似表徵也可能由量測偏差造成，因此應回到將分段測壓水位、孔口高程及量測深度換到共同基準，以獨立證據判別原因；只修補可見症狀將留下原本的傳力或滲流問題。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Confusing depth with head misestimates water pressure and water-control demand. Similar symptoms can arise from measurement bias: return to reduce interval heads, collar elevations and measurement depths to a common datum to discriminate the cause. Treating visible symptoms alone leaves the original transfer or seepage problem unresolved. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：判別這個機制時，應觀察將分段測壓水位、孔口高程及量測深度換到共同基準；若出現混用地表深度與水頭使設計水壓估錯，錯判止水需求，便須重新檢查原先假設的接觸、力或水的傳遞邊界，而不能只調整計算結果。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: If confusing depth with head misestimates water pressure and water-control demand, revisit the assumed contact, force or water-transfer boundary rather than merely adjusting the calculated result.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「隧道埋得多深就一定有完全相同的地下水頭」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Tunnel burial depth always equals the groundwater head\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b163-v14-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"混用地表深度與水頭使設計水壓估錯，錯判止水需求。相似表徵也可能由量測偏差造成，因此應回到將分段測壓水位、孔口高程及量測深度換到共同基準，以獨立證據判別原因；只修補可見症狀將留下原本的傳力或滲流問題。","textEn":"Confusing depth with head misestimates water pressure and water-control demand. Similar symptoms can arise from measurement bias: return to reduce interval heads, collar elevations and measurement depths to a common datum to discriminate the cause. Treating visible symptoms alone leaves the original transfer or seepage problem unresolved.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"]},{"id":"b163-v14-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「水頭基準與孔隙水壓」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Head datum and pore pressure\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","混用地表深度與水頭使設計水壓估錯，錯判止水需求。","泵表壓力永遠等於灌漿孔段實際壓力"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Confusing depth with head misestimates water pressure and water-control demand.","Pump-gauge pressure always equals actual pressure in the treated interval"],"answer":1,"explanation":"混用地表深度與水頭使設計水壓估錯，錯判止水需求。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Confusing depth with head misestimates water pressure and water-control demand. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b163-v14-05","title":"泵表讀值與孔段壓力：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Pump gauge and interval pressure: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b163-v14-04"],"objective":"說明「泵表讀值與孔段壓力」如何影響高水壓隧道止水灌漿的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Pump gauge and interval pressure” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Water-control grouting in high-pressure tunnels”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"泵表位置和目標孔段高程不同，管線摩擦及局部損失也使讀值不能直接當孔內壓力。壓差隨流量、材料和管路狀態改變，靜止時與流動時的校核意義不同；必須定義正負高程和壓力類型，避免重複扣除水頭。 判別這個機制時，應觀察以可用孔段壓力、流量及管路校核共同檢查泵表換算；若出現只讀泵表而忽略堵管損失，誤以為目標地層已受相同壓力，便須重新檢查原先假設的接觸、力或水的傳遞邊界，而不能只調整計算結果。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「泵表讀值與孔段壓力」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Gauge elevation differs from the target interval, while line and local losses prevent direct transfer of readings. Loss changes with flow, material and pipe condition, so static and flowing checks differ. Define elevation signs and pressure type to avoid counting head corrections twice. Use the following check to discriminate the mechanism: Check gauge conversion using available interval pressure, flow and line calibration. If ignoring line blockage losses falsely assigns gauge pressure to the target ground, revisit the assumed contact, force or water-transfer boundary rather than merely adjusting the calculated result. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Pump gauge and interval pressure” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：Inputs conveyed-fluid density=1000 kg/m3, g=9.81 m/s2, downward elevation change=10 m; pInterval=0.90 MPa+0.0981 MPa-0.15 MPa=0.8481 MPa; another grout density requires recalculating the hydrostatic term。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: Inputs conveyed-fluid density=1000 kg/m3, g=9.81 m/s2, downward elevation change=10 m; pInterval=0.90 MPa+0.0981 MPa-0.15 MPa=0.8481 MPa; another grout density requires recalculating the hydrostatic term.","failure":"常見誤解：「泵表壓力永遠等於灌漿孔段實際壓力」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Pump-gauge pressure always equals actual pressure in the treated interval\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「泵表讀值與孔段壓力」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Pump gauge and interval pressure”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b163-v14-05-k1","title":"泵表讀值與孔段壓力","titleEn":"Pump gauge and interval pressure","text":"泵表位置和目標孔段高程不同，管線摩擦及局部損失也使讀值不能直接當孔內壓力。壓差隨流量、材料和管路狀態改變，靜止時與流動時的校核意義不同；必須定義正負高程和壓力類型，避免重複扣除水頭。","textEn":"Gauge elevation differs from the target interval, while line and local losses prevent direct transfer of readings. Loss changes with flow, material and pipe condition, so static and flowing checks differ.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"]},{"id":"b163-v14-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：泵表壓力永遠等於灌漿孔段實際壓力 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Pump-gauge pressure always equals actual pressure in the treated interval Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「泵表讀值與孔段壓力」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Pump gauge and interval pressure\" is correct?","options":["泵表壓力永遠等於灌漿孔段實際壓力","淨注入壓差低就能保證任何地層都不會開裂","泵表位置和目標孔段高程不同，管線摩擦及局部損失也使讀值不能直接當孔內壓力。"],"optionsEn":["Pump-gauge pressure always equals actual pressure in the treated interval","A low net injection difference guarantees no ground can fracture","Gauge elevation differs from the target interval, while line and local losses prevent direct transfer of readings."],"answer":2,"explanation":"泵表位置和目標孔段高程不同，管線摩擦及局部損失也使讀值不能直接當孔內壓力。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Gauge elevation differs from the target interval, while line and local losses prevent direct transfer of readings. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b163-v14-06","title":"泵表讀值與孔段壓力：定量估算","titleEn":"Pump gauge and interval pressure: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b163-v14-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「泵表讀值與孔段壓力」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Pump gauge and interval pressure” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：Inputs conveyed-fluid density=1000 kg/m3, g=9.81 m/s2, downward elevation change=10 m; pInterval=0.90 MPa+0.0981 MPa-0.15 MPa=0.8481 MPa; another grout density requires recalculating the hydrostatic term。算例只描述水力關係，不提供現地配方、注入壓力或施作授權。 此結果僅用來核對量綱及模型敏感度，不是專案設計值、實測紀錄或現場允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: Inputs conveyed-fluid density=1000 kg/m3, g=9.81 m/s2, downward elevation change=10 m; pInterval=0.90 MPa+0.0981 MPa-0.15 MPa=0.8481 MPa; another grout density requires recalculating the hydrostatic term. Examples describe hydraulic relationships, not field recipes, injection pressures or operating authorization. This checks dimensions and model sensitivity; it is neither measured project data nor a design or acceptance value. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以可用孔段壓力、流量及管路校核共同檢查泵表換算。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check gauge conversion using available interval pressure, flow and line calibration.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b163-v14-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：Inputs conveyed-fluid density=1000 kg/m3, g=9.81 m/s2, downward elevation change=10 m; pInterval=0.90 MPa+0.0981 MPa-0.15 MPa=0.8481 MPa; another grout density requires recalculating the hydrostatic term。算例只描述水力關係，不提供現地配方、注入壓力或施作授權。 此結果僅用來核對量綱及模型敏感度，不是專案設計值、實測紀錄或現場允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Inputs conveyed-fluid density=1000 kg/m3, g=9.81 m/s2, downward elevation change=10 m; pInterval=0.90 MPa+0.0981 MPa-0.15 MPa=0.8481 MPa; another grout density requires recalculating the hydrostatic term. Examples describe hydraulic relationships, not field recipes, injection pressures or operating authorization. This checks dimensions and model sensitivity; it is neither measured project data nor a design or acceptance value.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"]},{"id":"b163-v14-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「泵表讀值與孔段壓力」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Pump gauge and interval pressure\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：Inputs conveyed-fluid density=1000 kg/m3, g=9.81 m/s2, downward elevation change=10 m; pInterval=0.90 MPa+0.0981 MPa-0.15 MPa=0.8481 MPa; another grout density requires recalculating the hydrostatic term。","注入量達理論體積就能證明處理半徑完全達成","處理後流量降低就一定全部來自灌漿改善"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: Inputs conveyed-fluid density=1000 kg/m3, g=9.81 m/s2, downward elevation change=10 m.","Delivered theoretical volume proves the complete treatment radius has been achieved","Every post-treatment flow decrease is entirely caused by grouting improvement"],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：Inputs conveyed-fluid density=1000 kg/m3, g=9.81 m/s2, downward elevation change=10 m; pInterval=0.90 MPa+0.0981 MPa-0.15 MPa=0.8481 MPa; another grout density requires recalculating the hydrostatic term。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Inputs conveyed-fluid density=1000 kg/m3, g=9.81 m/s2, downward elevation change=10 m; pInterval=0.90 MPa+0.0981 MPa-0.15 MPa=0.8481 MPa; another grout density requires recalculating the hydrostatic term. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b163-v14-07","title":"泵表讀值與孔段壓力：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Pump gauge and interval pressure: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b163-v14-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「泵表讀值與孔段壓力」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Pump gauge and interval pressure” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以可用孔段壓力、流量及管路校核共同檢查泵表換算。量測須保存位置、時間及基準，讓同條件的重複結果可比較；並特別檢查「只讀泵表而忽略堵管損失，誤以為目標地層已受相同壓力」是否能由這組資料區分。儀器校核與誤差估計應先於判讀，由負責技師核定該項試驗的允收和停留點。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check gauge conversion using available interval pressure, flow and line calibration. Retain position, time and datums for comparable repeats, specifically distinguishing this scenario: Ignoring line blockage losses falsely assigns gauge pressure to the target ground. Instrument checks and uncertainty estimates precede interpretation; the responsible engineer sets acceptance and hold points for this test. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將以可用孔段壓力、流量及管路校核共同檢查泵表換算列為該構件的交接證據，連結到施工位置、材料批次及判讀版本。若發現只讀泵表而忽略堵管損失，誤以為目標地層已受相同壓力，先保留原始紀錄並由負責技師確認處置，不能以本課算例替代核定作業計畫。","observationEn":"Site practice: Apply the following check at handover: Check gauge conversion using available interval pressure, flow and line calibration. Link results to location, material batch and interpretation version. If ignoring line blockage losses falsely assigns gauge pressure to the target ground, retain original records and obtain the responsible engineer's disposition; this example does not replace an approved work plan.","failure":"注意干擾：只讀泵表而忽略堵管損失，誤以為目標地層已受相同壓力。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Ignoring line blockage losses falsely assigns gauge pressure to the target ground. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b163-v14-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以可用孔段壓力、流量及管路校核共同檢查泵表換算。量測須保存位置、時間及基準，讓同條件的重複結果可比較；並特別檢查「只讀泵表而忽略堵管損失，誤以為目標地層已受相同壓力」是否能由這組資料區分。儀器校核與誤差估計應先於判讀，由負責技師核定該項試驗的允收和停留點。","textEn":"Check gauge conversion using available interval pressure, flow and line calibration. Retain position, time and datums for comparable repeats, specifically distinguishing this scenario: Ignoring line blockage losses falsely assigns gauge pressure to the target ground. Instrument checks and uncertainty estimates precede interpretation; the responsible engineer sets acceptance and hold points for this test.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"]},{"id":"b163-v14-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將以可用孔段壓力、流量及管路校核共同檢查泵表換算列為該構件的交接證據，連結到施工位置、材料批次及判讀版本。若發現只讀泵表而忽略堵管損失，誤以為目標地層已受相同壓力，先保留原始紀錄並由負責技師確認處置，不能以本課算例替代核定作業計畫。","textEn":"Apply the following check at handover: Check gauge conversion using available interval pressure, flow and line calibration. Link results to location, material batch and interpretation version. If ignoring line blockage losses falsely assigns gauge pressure to the target ground, retain original records and obtain the responsible engineer's disposition; this example does not replace an approved work plan.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「泵表讀值與孔段壓力」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Pump gauge and interval pressure\"?","options":["沿用另一條隧道或另一處地層的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","以可用孔段壓力、流量及管路校核共同檢查泵表換算。","施工後短期不漏就代表材料永遠不會劣化"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another tunnel or ground formation counts as verifying this structure.","Check gauge conversion using available interval pressure, flow and line calibration.","Initial absence of leakage proves the material will never deteriorate"],"answer":1,"explanation":"以可用孔段壓力、流量及管路校核共同檢查泵表換算。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check gauge conversion using available interval pressure, flow and line calibration. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b163-v14-08","title":"泵表讀值與孔段壓力：失效診斷","titleEn":"Pump gauge and interval pressure: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b163-v14-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「泵表讀值與孔段壓力」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Pump gauge and interval pressure” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只讀泵表而忽略堵管損失，誤以為目標地層已受相同壓力。相似表徵也可能由量測偏差造成，因此應回到以可用孔段壓力、流量及管路校核共同檢查泵表換算，以獨立證據判別原因；只修補可見症狀將留下原本的傳力或滲流問題。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Ignoring line blockage losses falsely assigns gauge pressure to the target ground. Similar symptoms can arise from measurement bias: return to check gauge conversion using available interval pressure, flow and line calibration to discriminate the cause. Treating visible symptoms alone leaves the original transfer or seepage problem unresolved. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：判別這個機制時，應觀察以可用孔段壓力、流量及管路校核共同檢查泵表換算；若出現只讀泵表而忽略堵管損失，誤以為目標地層已受相同壓力，便須重新檢查原先假設的接觸、力或水的傳遞邊界，而不能只調整計算結果。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: If ignoring line blockage losses falsely assigns gauge pressure to the target ground, revisit the assumed contact, force or water-transfer boundary rather than merely adjusting the calculated result.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「泵表壓力永遠等於灌漿孔段實際壓力」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Pump-gauge pressure always equals actual pressure in the treated interval\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b163-v14-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只讀泵表而忽略堵管損失，誤以為目標地層已受相同壓力。相似表徵也可能由量測偏差造成，因此應回到以可用孔段壓力、流量及管路校核共同檢查泵表換算，以獨立證據判別原因；只修補可見症狀將留下原本的傳力或滲流問題。","textEn":"Ignoring line blockage losses falsely assigns gauge pressure to the target ground. Similar symptoms can arise from measurement bias: return to check gauge conversion using available interval pressure, flow and line calibration to discriminate the cause. Treating visible symptoms alone leaves the original transfer or seepage problem unresolved.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"]},{"id":"b163-v14-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「泵表讀值與孔段壓力」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Pump gauge and interval pressure\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","淨注入壓差低就能保證任何地層都不會開裂","只讀泵表而忽略堵管損失，誤以為目標地層已受相同壓力。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","A low net injection difference guarantees no ground can fracture","Ignoring line blockage losses falsely assigns gauge pressure to the target ground."],"answer":2,"explanation":"只讀泵表而忽略堵管損失，誤以為目標地層已受相同壓力。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Ignoring line blockage losses falsely assigns gauge pressure to the target ground. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b163-v14-s2","title":"機制、材料與定量設計","titleEn":"Mechanisms, materials and quantitative design","description":"本階段聚焦「孔隙壓與有效作用差」與「裂隙開度與流量敏感度」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Pore pressure and net pressure difference\" and \"Fracture aperture and flow sensitivity\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b163-v14-09","title":"孔隙壓與有效作用差：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Pore pressure and net pressure difference: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b163-v14-08"],"objective":"說明「孔隙壓與有效作用差」如何影響高水壓隧道止水灌漿的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Pore pressure and net pressure difference” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Water-control grouting in high-pressure tunnels”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"注入端壓力與原地下水壓之差影響流動，但不能單獨決定地層是否會開裂或抬升。最小主應力、既有裂隙與連通路徑同樣重要，局部壓力還可能傳到遠處薄弱面；模型應區分水力驅動差與允許作用上限。 判別這個機制時，應觀察對照孔段壓差、周邊位移及相鄰測壓反應；若出現把淨壓差小誤當無風險，忽略遠處低拘束裂隙開啟，便須重新檢查原先假設的接觸、力或水的傳遞邊界，而不能只調整計算結果。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「孔隙壓與有效作用差」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The difference between injection and groundwater pressure drives flow but does not alone establish fracture or uplift risk. Minimum stress, existing joints and connectivity also matter, with pressure reaching remote weak planes. Distinguish a hydraulic driving difference from an allowable action limit. Use the following check to discriminate the mechanism: Compare interval pressure difference with surrounding movement and neighbouring head responses. If a small net difference is treated as risk-free despite remote low-restraint joints opening, revisit the assumed contact, force or water-transfer boundary rather than merely adjusting the calculated result. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Pore pressure and net pressure difference” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：netDifference=0.8481 MPa-0.7848 MPa=0.0633 MPa=63.3 kPa。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: netDifference=0.8481 MPa-0.7848 MPa=0.0633 MPa=63.3 kPa.","failure":"常見誤解：「淨注入壓差低就能保證任何地層都不會開裂」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A low net injection difference guarantees no ground can fracture\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「孔隙壓與有效作用差」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Pore pressure and net pressure difference”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b163-v14-09-k1","title":"孔隙壓與有效作用差","titleEn":"Pore pressure and net pressure difference","text":"注入端壓力與原地下水壓之差影響流動，但不能單獨決定地層是否會開裂或抬升。最小主應力、既有裂隙與連通路徑同樣重要，局部壓力還可能傳到遠處薄弱面；模型應區分水力驅動差與允許作用上限。","textEn":"The difference between injection and groundwater pressure drives flow but does not alone establish fracture or uplift risk. Minimum stress, existing joints and connectivity also matter, with pressure reaching remote weak planes.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"]},{"id":"b163-v14-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：淨注入壓差低就能保證任何地層都不會開裂 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A low net injection difference guarantees no ground can fracture Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「孔隙壓與有效作用差」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Pore pressure and net pressure difference\" is correct?","options":["注入端壓力與原地下水壓之差影響流動，但不能單獨決定地層是否會開裂或抬升。","淨注入壓差低就能保證任何地層都不會開裂","所有裂隙對總漏水的貢獻都大致相同"],"optionsEn":["The difference between injection and groundwater pressure drives flow but does not alone establish fracture or uplift risk.","A low net injection difference guarantees no ground can fracture","Every fracture contributes approximately equally to total leakage"],"answer":0,"explanation":"注入端壓力與原地下水壓之差影響流動，但不能單獨決定地層是否會開裂或抬升。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The difference between injection and groundwater pressure drives flow but does not alone establish fracture or uplift risk. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b163-v14-10","title":"孔隙壓與有效作用差：定量估算","titleEn":"Pore pressure and net pressure difference: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b163-v14-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「孔隙壓與有效作用差」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Pore pressure and net pressure difference” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：netDifference=0.8481 MPa-0.7848 MPa=0.0633 MPa=63.3 kPa。算例只描述水力關係，不提供現地配方、注入壓力或施作授權。 此結果僅用來核對量綱及模型敏感度，不是專案設計值、實測紀錄或現場允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: netDifference=0.8481 MPa-0.7848 MPa=0.0633 MPa=63.3 kPa. Examples describe hydraulic relationships, not field recipes, injection pressures or operating authorization. This checks dimensions and model sensitivity; it is neither measured project data nor a design or acceptance value. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：對照孔段壓差、周邊位移及相鄰測壓反應。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare interval pressure difference with surrounding movement and neighbouring head responses.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b163-v14-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：netDifference=0.8481 MPa-0.7848 MPa=0.0633 MPa=63.3 kPa。算例只描述水力關係，不提供現地配方、注入壓力或施作授權。 此結果僅用來核對量綱及模型敏感度，不是專案設計值、實測紀錄或現場允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: netDifference=0.8481 MPa-0.7848 MPa=0.0633 MPa=63.3 kPa. Examples describe hydraulic relationships, not field recipes, injection pressures or operating authorization. This checks dimensions and model sensitivity; it is neither measured project data nor a design or acceptance value.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"]},{"id":"b163-v14-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「孔隙壓與有效作用差」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Pore pressure and net pressure difference\", which statement holds?","options":["入口壓力升高就能證明整個處理區都已封閉","原創教學假設：netDifference=0.8481 MPa-0.7848 MPa=0.0633 MPa=63.3 kPa。","孔口周圍沒變形就能證明所有遠端地層都沒反應"],"optionsEn":["Rising entrance pressure proves the entire treated zone is sealed","Original teaching assumptions: netDifference=0.8481 MPa-0.7848 MPa=0.0633 MPa=63.3 kPa.","No movement near the collar proves all distant ground remains unaffected"],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：netDifference=0.8481 MPa-0.7848 MPa=0.0633 MPa=63.3 kPa。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: netDifference=0.8481 MPa-0.7848 MPa=0.0633 MPa=63.3 kPa. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b163-v14-11","title":"孔隙壓與有效作用差：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Pore pressure and net pressure difference: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b163-v14-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「孔隙壓與有效作用差」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Pore pressure and net pressure difference” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"對照孔段壓差、周邊位移及相鄰測壓反應。量測須保存位置、時間及基準，讓同條件的重複結果可比較；並特別檢查「把淨壓差小誤當無風險，忽略遠處低拘束裂隙開啟」是否能由這組資料區分。儀器校核與誤差估計應先於判讀，由負責技師核定該項試驗的允收和停留點。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare interval pressure difference with surrounding movement and neighbouring head responses. Retain position, time and datums for comparable repeats, specifically distinguishing this scenario: A small net difference is treated as risk-free despite remote low-restraint joints opening. Instrument checks and uncertainty estimates precede interpretation; the responsible engineer sets acceptance and hold points for this test. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將對照孔段壓差、周邊位移及相鄰測壓反應列為該構件的交接證據，連結到施工位置、材料批次及判讀版本。若發現把淨壓差小誤當無風險，忽略遠處低拘束裂隙開啟，先保留原始紀錄並由負責技師確認處置，不能以本課算例替代核定作業計畫。","observationEn":"Site practice: Apply the following check at handover: Compare interval pressure difference with surrounding movement and neighbouring head responses. Link results to location, material batch and interpretation version. If a small net difference is treated as risk-free despite remote low-restraint joints opening, retain original records and obtain the responsible engineer's disposition; this example does not replace an approved work plan.","failure":"注意干擾：把淨壓差小誤當無風險，忽略遠處低拘束裂隙開啟。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A small net difference is treated as risk-free despite remote low-restraint joints opening. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b163-v14-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"對照孔段壓差、周邊位移及相鄰測壓反應。量測須保存位置、時間及基準，讓同條件的重複結果可比較；並特別檢查「把淨壓差小誤當無風險，忽略遠處低拘束裂隙開啟」是否能由這組資料區分。儀器校核與誤差估計應先於判讀，由負責技師核定該項試驗的允收和停留點。","textEn":"Compare interval pressure difference with surrounding movement and neighbouring head responses. Retain position, time and datums for comparable repeats, specifically distinguishing this scenario: A small net difference is treated as risk-free despite remote low-restraint joints opening. Instrument checks and uncertainty estimates precede interpretation; the responsible engineer sets acceptance and hold points for this test.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"]},{"id":"b163-v14-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將對照孔段壓差、周邊位移及相鄰測壓反應列為該構件的交接證據，連結到施工位置、材料批次及判讀版本。若發現把淨壓差小誤當無風險，忽略遠處低拘束裂隙開啟，先保留原始紀錄並由負責技師確認處置，不能以本課算例替代核定作業計畫。","textEn":"Apply the following check at handover: Compare interval pressure difference with surrounding movement and neighbouring head responses. Link results to location, material batch and interpretation version. If a small net difference is treated as risk-free despite remote low-restraint joints opening, retain original records and obtain the responsible engineer's disposition; this example does not replace an approved work plan.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「孔隙壓與有效作用差」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Pore pressure and net pressure difference\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","中心驗證孔合格就能代表整個止水範圍連續","對照孔段壓差、周邊位移及相鄰測壓反應。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","A passing central verification hole proves the entire water barrier is continuous","Compare interval pressure difference with surrounding movement and neighbouring head responses."],"answer":2,"explanation":"對照孔段壓差、周邊位移及相鄰測壓反應。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare interval pressure difference with surrounding movement and neighbouring head responses. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b163-v14-12","title":"孔隙壓與有效作用差：失效診斷","titleEn":"Pore pressure and net pressure difference: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b163-v14-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「孔隙壓與有效作用差」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Pore pressure and net pressure difference” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把淨壓差小誤當無風險，忽略遠處低拘束裂隙開啟。相似表徵也可能由量測偏差造成，因此應回到對照孔段壓差、周邊位移及相鄰測壓反應，以獨立證據判別原因；只修補可見症狀將留下原本的傳力或滲流問題。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A small net difference is treated as risk-free despite remote low-restraint joints opening. Similar symptoms can arise from measurement bias: return to compare interval pressure difference with surrounding movement and neighbouring head responses to discriminate the cause. Treating visible symptoms alone leaves the original transfer or seepage problem unresolved. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：判別這個機制時，應觀察對照孔段壓差、周邊位移及相鄰測壓反應；若出現把淨壓差小誤當無風險，忽略遠處低拘束裂隙開啟，便須重新檢查原先假設的接觸、力或水的傳遞邊界，而不能只調整計算結果。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: If a small net difference is treated as risk-free despite remote low-restraint joints opening, revisit the assumed contact, force or water-transfer boundary rather than merely adjusting the calculated result.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「淨注入壓差低就能保證任何地層都不會開裂」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A low net injection difference guarantees no ground can fracture\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b163-v14-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把淨壓差小誤當無風險，忽略遠處低拘束裂隙開啟。相似表徵也可能由量測偏差造成，因此應回到對照孔段壓差、周邊位移及相鄰測壓反應，以獨立證據判別原因；只修補可見症狀將留下原本的傳力或滲流問題。","textEn":"A small net difference is treated as risk-free despite remote low-restraint joints opening. Similar symptoms can arise from measurement bias: return to compare interval pressure difference with surrounding movement and neighbouring head responses to discriminate the cause. Treating visible symptoms alone leaves the original transfer or seepage problem unresolved.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"]},{"id":"b163-v14-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「孔隙壓與有效作用差」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Pore pressure and net pressure difference\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["把淨壓差小誤當無風險，忽略遠處低拘束裂隙開啟。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","所有裂隙對總漏水的貢獻都大致相同"],"optionsEn":["A small net difference is treated as risk-free despite remote low-restraint joints opening.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Every fracture contributes approximately equally to total leakage"],"answer":0,"explanation":"把淨壓差小誤當無風險，忽略遠處低拘束裂隙開啟。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A small net difference is treated as risk-free despite remote low-restraint joints opening. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b163-v14-13","title":"裂隙開度與流量敏感度：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Fracture aperture and flow sensitivity: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b163-v14-12"],"objective":"說明「裂隙開度與流量敏感度」如何影響高水壓隧道止水灌漿的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Fracture aperture and flow sensitivity” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Water-control grouting in high-pressure tunnels”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"理想平行板層流的流量對開度立方敏感，微小開合可大幅改變流量。天然裂隙粗糙、分岔且有接觸點，不能從一個流量唯一反算開度；此模型適合解釋為何少數連通裂隙可能主導整體漏水。 判別這個機制時，應觀察在可比水頭下比較分段流量與裂隙連通證據；若出現只封小裂隙卻漏掉主通道，總流量改善有限，便須重新檢查原先假設的接觸、力或水的傳遞邊界，而不能只調整計算結果。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「裂隙開度與流量敏感度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Ideal parallel-plate laminar flow varies with aperture cubed, so small changes can strongly alter discharge. Natural joints are rough, branching and partly contacting, preventing unique aperture inference from one flow. The model explains why a few connected fractures can dominate leakage. Use the following check to discriminate the mechanism: Compare interval flow and fracture connectivity at comparable heads. If sealing minor cracks while missing the main pathway gives little total-flow improvement, revisit the assumed contact, force or water-transfer boundary rather than merely adjusting the calculated result. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Fracture aperture and flow sensitivity” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：flowRatio=(newAperture/oldAperture)^3=(1.1)^3=1.331。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: flowRatio=(newAperture/oldAperture)^3=(1.1)^3=1.331.","failure":"常見誤解：「所有裂隙對總漏水的貢獻都大致相同」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Every fracture contributes approximately equally to total leakage\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「裂隙開度與流量敏感度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Fracture aperture and flow sensitivity”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b163-v14-13-k1","title":"裂隙開度與流量敏感度","titleEn":"Fracture aperture and flow sensitivity","text":"理想平行板層流的流量對開度立方敏感，微小開合可大幅改變流量。天然裂隙粗糙、分岔且有接觸點，不能從一個流量唯一反算開度；此模型適合解釋為何少數連通裂隙可能主導整體漏水。","textEn":"Ideal parallel-plate laminar flow varies with aperture cubed, so small changes can strongly alter discharge. Natural joints are rough, branching and partly contacting, preventing unique aperture inference from one flow.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"]},{"id":"b163-v14-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：所有裂隙對總漏水的貢獻都大致相同 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Every fracture contributes approximately equally to total leakage Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「裂隙開度與流量敏感度」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Fracture aperture and flow sensitivity\" is correct?","options":["所有裂隙對總漏水的貢獻都大致相同","理想平行板層流的流量對開度立方敏感，微小開合可大幅改變流量。","注入量達理論體積就能證明處理半徑完全達成"],"optionsEn":["Every fracture contributes approximately equally to total leakage","Ideal parallel-plate laminar flow varies with aperture cubed, so small changes can strongly alter discharge.","Delivered theoretical volume proves the complete treatment radius has been achieved"],"answer":1,"explanation":"理想平行板層流的流量對開度立方敏感，微小開合可大幅改變流量。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Ideal parallel-plate laminar flow varies with aperture cubed, so small changes can strongly alter discharge. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b163-v14-14","title":"裂隙開度與流量敏感度：定量估算","titleEn":"Fracture aperture and flow sensitivity: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b163-v14-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「裂隙開度與流量敏感度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Fracture aperture and flow sensitivity” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：flowRatio=(newAperture/oldAperture)^3=(1.1)^3=1.331。算例只描述水力關係，不提供現地配方、注入壓力或施作授權。 此結果僅用來核對量綱及模型敏感度，不是專案設計值、實測紀錄或現場允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: flowRatio=(newAperture/oldAperture)^3=(1.1)^3=1.331. Examples describe hydraulic relationships, not field recipes, injection pressures or operating authorization. This checks dimensions and model sensitivity; it is neither measured project data nor a design or acceptance value. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在可比水頭下比較分段流量與裂隙連通證據。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare interval flow and fracture connectivity at comparable heads.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b163-v14-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：flowRatio=(newAperture/oldAperture)^3=(1.1)^3=1.331。算例只描述水力關係，不提供現地配方、注入壓力或施作授權。 此結果僅用來核對量綱及模型敏感度，不是專案設計值、實測紀錄或現場允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: flowRatio=(newAperture/oldAperture)^3=(1.1)^3=1.331. Examples describe hydraulic relationships, not field recipes, injection pressures or operating authorization. This checks dimensions and model sensitivity; it is neither measured project data nor a design or acceptance value.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"]},{"id":"b163-v14-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「裂隙開度與流量敏感度」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Fracture aperture and flow sensitivity\", which statement holds?","options":["處理後流量降低就一定全部來自灌漿改善","施工後短期不漏就代表材料永遠不會劣化","原創教學假設：flowRatio=(newAperture/oldAperture)^3=(1.1)^3=1.331。"],"optionsEn":["Every post-treatment flow decrease is entirely caused by grouting improvement","Initial absence of leakage proves the material will never deteriorate","Original teaching assumptions: flowRatio=(newAperture/oldAperture)^3=(1.1)^3=1.331."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：flowRatio=(newAperture/oldAperture)^3=(1.1)^3=1.331。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: flowRatio=(newAperture/oldAperture)^3=(1.1)^3=1.331. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b163-v14-15","title":"裂隙開度與流量敏感度：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Fracture aperture and flow sensitivity: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b163-v14-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「裂隙開度與流量敏感度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Fracture aperture and flow sensitivity” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在可比水頭下比較分段流量與裂隙連通證據。量測須保存位置、時間及基準，讓同條件的重複結果可比較；並特別檢查「只封小裂隙卻漏掉主通道，總流量改善有限」是否能由這組資料區分。儀器校核與誤差估計應先於判讀，由負責技師核定該項試驗的允收和停留點。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare interval flow and fracture connectivity at comparable heads. Retain position, time and datums for comparable repeats, specifically distinguishing this scenario: Sealing minor cracks while missing the main pathway gives little total-flow improvement. Instrument checks and uncertainty estimates precede interpretation; the responsible engineer sets acceptance and hold points for this test. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將在可比水頭下比較分段流量與裂隙連通證據列為該構件的交接證據，連結到施工位置、材料批次及判讀版本。若發現只封小裂隙卻漏掉主通道，總流量改善有限，先保留原始紀錄並由負責技師確認處置，不能以本課算例替代核定作業計畫。","observationEn":"Site practice: Apply the following check at handover: Compare interval flow and fracture connectivity at comparable heads. Link results to location, material batch and interpretation version. If sealing minor cracks while missing the main pathway gives little total-flow improvement, retain original records and obtain the responsible engineer's disposition; this example does not replace an approved work plan.","failure":"注意干擾：只封小裂隙卻漏掉主通道，總流量改善有限。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Sealing minor cracks while missing the main pathway gives little total-flow improvement. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b163-v14-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在可比水頭下比較分段流量與裂隙連通證據。量測須保存位置、時間及基準，讓同條件的重複結果可比較；並特別檢查「只封小裂隙卻漏掉主通道，總流量改善有限」是否能由這組資料區分。儀器校核與誤差估計應先於判讀，由負責技師核定該項試驗的允收和停留點。","textEn":"Compare interval flow and fracture connectivity at comparable heads. Retain position, time and datums for comparable repeats, specifically distinguishing this scenario: Sealing minor cracks while missing the main pathway gives little total-flow improvement. Instrument checks and uncertainty estimates precede interpretation; the responsible engineer sets acceptance and hold points for this test.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"]},{"id":"b163-v14-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將在可比水頭下比較分段流量與裂隙連通證據列為該構件的交接證據，連結到施工位置、材料批次及判讀版本。若發現只封小裂隙卻漏掉主通道，總流量改善有限，先保留原始紀錄並由負責技師確認處置，不能以本課算例替代核定作業計畫。","textEn":"Apply the following check at handover: Compare interval flow and fracture connectivity at comparable heads. Link results to location, material batch and interpretation version. If sealing minor cracks while missing the main pathway gives little total-flow improvement, retain original records and obtain the responsible engineer's disposition; this example does not replace an approved work plan.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「裂隙開度與流量敏感度」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Fracture aperture and flow sensitivity\"?","options":["在可比水頭下比較分段流量與裂隙連通證據。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","隧道埋得多深就一定有完全相同的地下水頭"],"optionsEn":["Compare interval flow and fracture connectivity at comparable heads.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Tunnel burial depth always equals the groundwater head"],"answer":0,"explanation":"在可比水頭下比較分段流量與裂隙連通證據。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare interval flow and fracture connectivity at comparable heads. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b163-v14-16","title":"裂隙開度與流量敏感度：失效診斷","titleEn":"Fracture aperture and flow sensitivity: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b163-v14-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「裂隙開度與流量敏感度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Fracture aperture and flow sensitivity” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只封小裂隙卻漏掉主通道，總流量改善有限。相似表徵也可能由量測偏差造成，因此應回到在可比水頭下比較分段流量與裂隙連通證據，以獨立證據判別原因；只修補可見症狀將留下原本的傳力或滲流問題。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Sealing minor cracks while missing the main pathway gives little total-flow improvement. Similar symptoms can arise from measurement bias: return to compare interval flow and fracture connectivity at comparable heads to discriminate the cause. Treating visible symptoms alone leaves the original transfer or seepage problem unresolved. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：判別這個機制時，應觀察在可比水頭下比較分段流量與裂隙連通證據；若出現只封小裂隙卻漏掉主通道，總流量改善有限，便須重新檢查原先假設的接觸、力或水的傳遞邊界，而不能只調整計算結果。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: If sealing minor cracks while missing the main pathway gives little total-flow improvement, revisit the assumed contact, force or water-transfer boundary rather than merely adjusting the calculated result.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「所有裂隙對總漏水的貢獻都大致相同」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Every fracture contributes approximately equally to total leakage\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b163-v14-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只封小裂隙卻漏掉主通道，總流量改善有限。相似表徵也可能由量測偏差造成，因此應回到在可比水頭下比較分段流量與裂隙連通證據，以獨立證據判別原因；只修補可見症狀將留下原本的傳力或滲流問題。","textEn":"Sealing minor cracks while missing the main pathway gives little total-flow improvement. Similar symptoms can arise from measurement bias: return to compare interval flow and fracture connectivity at comparable heads to discriminate the cause. Treating visible symptoms alone leaves the original transfer or seepage problem unresolved.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"]},{"id":"b163-v14-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「裂隙開度與流量敏感度」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Fracture aperture and flow sensitivity\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","只封小裂隙卻漏掉主通道，總流量改善有限。","注入量達理論體積就能證明處理半徑完全達成"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Sealing minor cracks while missing the main pathway gives little total-flow improvement.","Delivered theoretical volume proves the complete treatment radius has been achieved"],"answer":1,"explanation":"只封小裂隙卻漏掉主通道，總流量改善有限。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Sealing minor cracks while missing the main pathway gives little total-flow improvement. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b163-v14-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「幾何體積與實際注入量」與「材料可灌性與粒徑」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Geometric volume and delivered volume\" and \"Grout penetrability and particle size\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b163-v14-17","title":"幾何體積與實際注入量：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Geometric volume and delivered volume: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b163-v14-16"],"objective":"說明「幾何體積與實際注入量」如何影響高水壓隧道止水灌漿的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Geometric volume and delivered volume” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Water-control grouting in high-pressure tunnels”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"理想處理環體積可作材料帳基準，但地層不是均勻多孔體，注入可能集中在少數通道。超過理論體積並不證明處理半徑增加，可能是外逸或相鄰孔連通；必須把材料去向和地下水反應一起辨認。 判別這個機制時，應觀察將注入收支、相鄰孔反應及可見逸流位置共同索引；若出現大量外逸被當成有效填充，留下未處理的高滲區，便須重新檢查原先假設的接觸、力或水的傳遞邊界，而不能只調整計算結果。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「幾何體積與實際注入量」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"An ideal treatment annulus offers a volume baseline, but ground is not a uniform porous medium and delivery may concentrate in a few channels. Excess volume does not prove a larger treatment radius; it may escape or connect to another hole. Interpret material destinations with groundwater response. Use the following check to discriminate the mechanism: Index delivered balance, neighbouring-hole responses and visible escape locations together. If large losses are credited as useful filling while high-permeability zones remain untreated, revisit the assumed contact, force or water-transfer boundary rather than merely adjusting the calculated result. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Geometric volume and delivered volume” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：Inputs r=0.5 m, r0=0.05 m, L=3 m, assumedConnectedVoidFraction=0.10; V=pi*(r^2-r0^2)*L*n=pi*(0.5^2-0.05^2)*3*0.10=0.233 m3。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: Inputs r=0.5 m, r0=0.05 m, L=3 m, assumedConnectedVoidFraction=0.10; V=pi*(r^2-r0^2)*L*n=pi*(0.5^2-0.05^2)*3*0.10=0.233 m3.","failure":"常見誤解：「注入量達理論體積就能證明處理半徑完全達成」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Delivered theoretical volume proves the complete treatment radius has been achieved\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「幾何體積與實際注入量」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Geometric volume and delivered volume”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b163-v14-17-k1","title":"幾何體積與實際注入量","titleEn":"Geometric volume and delivered volume","text":"理想處理環體積可作材料帳基準，但地層不是均勻多孔體，注入可能集中在少數通道。超過理論體積並不證明處理半徑增加，可能是外逸或相鄰孔連通；必須把材料去向和地下水反應一起辨認。","textEn":"An ideal treatment annulus offers a volume baseline, but ground is not a uniform porous medium and delivery may concentrate in a few channels. Excess volume does not prove a larger treatment radius; it may escape or connect to another hole.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"]},{"id":"b163-v14-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：注入量達理論體積就能證明處理半徑完全達成 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Delivered theoretical volume proves the complete treatment radius has been achieved Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「幾何體積與實際注入量」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Geometric volume and delivered volume\" is correct?","options":["注入量達理論體積就能證明處理半徑完全達成","入口壓力升高就能證明整個處理區都已封閉","理想處理環體積可作材料帳基準，但地層不是均勻多孔體，注入可能集中在少數通道。"],"optionsEn":["Delivered theoretical volume proves the complete treatment radius has been achieved","Rising entrance pressure proves the entire treated zone is sealed","An ideal treatment annulus offers a volume baseline, but ground is not a uniform porous medium and delivery may concentrate in a few channels."],"answer":2,"explanation":"理想處理環體積可作材料帳基準，但地層不是均勻多孔體，注入可能集中在少數通道。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"An ideal treatment annulus offers a volume baseline, but ground is not a uniform porous medium and delivery may concentrate in a few channels. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b163-v14-18","title":"幾何體積與實際注入量：定量估算","titleEn":"Geometric volume and delivered volume: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b163-v14-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「幾何體積與實際注入量」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Geometric volume and delivered volume” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：Inputs r=0.5 m, r0=0.05 m, L=3 m, assumedConnectedVoidFraction=0.10; V=pi*(r^2-r0^2)*L*n=pi*(0.5^2-0.05^2)*3*0.10=0.233 m3。算例只描述水力關係，不提供現地配方、注入壓力或施作授權。 此結果僅用來核對量綱及模型敏感度，不是專案設計值、實測紀錄或現場允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: Inputs r=0.5 m, r0=0.05 m, L=3 m, assumedConnectedVoidFraction=0.10; V=pi*(r^2-r0^2)*L*n=pi*(0.5^2-0.05^2)*3*0.10=0.233 m3. Examples describe hydraulic relationships, not field recipes, injection pressures or operating authorization. This checks dimensions and model sensitivity; it is neither measured project data nor a design or acceptance value. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將注入收支、相鄰孔反應及可見逸流位置共同索引。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Index delivered balance, neighbouring-hole responses and visible escape locations together.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b163-v14-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：Inputs r=0.5 m, r0=0.05 m, L=3 m, assumedConnectedVoidFraction=0.10; V=pi*(r^2-r0^2)*L*n=pi*(0.5^2-0.05^2)*3*0.10=0.233 m3。算例只描述水力關係，不提供現地配方、注入壓力或施作授權。 此結果僅用來核對量綱及模型敏感度，不是專案設計值、實測紀錄或現場允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Inputs r=0.5 m, r0=0.05 m, L=3 m, assumedConnectedVoidFraction=0.10; V=pi*(r^2-r0^2)*L*n=pi*(0.5^2-0.05^2)*3*0.10=0.233 m3. Examples describe hydraulic relationships, not field recipes, injection pressures or operating authorization. This checks dimensions and model sensitivity; it is neither measured project data nor a design or acceptance value.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"]},{"id":"b163-v14-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「幾何體積與實際注入量」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Geometric volume and delivered volume\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：Inputs r=0.5 m, r0=0.05 m, L=3 m, assumedConnectedVoidFraction=0.10; V=pi*(r^2-r0^2)*L*n=pi*(0.5^2-0.05^2)*3*0.10=0.233 m3。","孔口周圍沒變形就能證明所有遠端地層都沒反應","中心驗證孔合格就能代表整個止水範圍連續"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: Inputs r=0.5 m, r0=0.05 m, L=3 m, assumedConnectedVoidFraction=0.10; V=pi*(r^2-r0^2)*L*n=pi*(0.5^2-0.05^2)*3*0.10=0.233 m3.","No movement near the collar proves all distant ground remains unaffected","A passing central verification hole proves the entire water barrier is continuous"],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：Inputs r=0.5 m, r0=0.05 m, L=3 m, assumedConnectedVoidFraction=0.10; V=pi*(r^2-r0^2)*L*n=pi*(0.5^2-0.05^2)*3*0.10=0.233 m3。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Inputs r=0.5 m, r0=0.05 m, L=3 m, assumedConnectedVoidFraction=0.10; V=pi*(r^2-r0^2)*L*n=pi*(0.5^2-0.05^2)*3*0.10=0.233 m3. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b163-v14-19","title":"幾何體積與實際注入量：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Geometric volume and delivered volume: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b163-v14-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「幾何體積與實際注入量」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Geometric volume and delivered volume” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將注入收支、相鄰孔反應及可見逸流位置共同索引。量測須保存位置、時間及基準，讓同條件的重複結果可比較；並特別檢查「大量外逸被當成有效填充，留下未處理的高滲區」是否能由這組資料區分。儀器校核與誤差估計應先於判讀，由負責技師核定該項試驗的允收和停留點。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Index delivered balance, neighbouring-hole responses and visible escape locations together. Retain position, time and datums for comparable repeats, specifically distinguishing this scenario: Large losses are credited as useful filling while high-permeability zones remain untreated. Instrument checks and uncertainty estimates precede interpretation; the responsible engineer sets acceptance and hold points for this test. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將將注入收支、相鄰孔反應及可見逸流位置共同索引列為該構件的交接證據，連結到施工位置、材料批次及判讀版本。若發現大量外逸被當成有效填充，留下未處理的高滲區，先保留原始紀錄並由負責技師確認處置，不能以本課算例替代核定作業計畫。","observationEn":"Site practice: Apply the following check at handover: Index delivered balance, neighbouring-hole responses and visible escape locations together. Link results to location, material batch and interpretation version. If large losses are credited as useful filling while high-permeability zones remain untreated, retain original records and obtain the responsible engineer's disposition; this example does not replace an approved work plan.","failure":"注意干擾：大量外逸被當成有效填充，留下未處理的高滲區。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Large losses are credited as useful filling while high-permeability zones remain untreated. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b163-v14-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將注入收支、相鄰孔反應及可見逸流位置共同索引。量測須保存位置、時間及基準，讓同條件的重複結果可比較；並特別檢查「大量外逸被當成有效填充，留下未處理的高滲區」是否能由這組資料區分。儀器校核與誤差估計應先於判讀，由負責技師核定該項試驗的允收和停留點。","textEn":"Index delivered balance, neighbouring-hole responses and visible escape locations together. Retain position, time and datums for comparable repeats, specifically distinguishing this scenario: Large losses are credited as useful filling while high-permeability zones remain untreated. Instrument checks and uncertainty estimates precede interpretation; the responsible engineer sets acceptance and hold points for this test.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"]},{"id":"b163-v14-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將將注入收支、相鄰孔反應及可見逸流位置共同索引列為該構件的交接證據，連結到施工位置、材料批次及判讀版本。若發現大量外逸被當成有效填充，留下未處理的高滲區，先保留原始紀錄並由負責技師確認處置，不能以本課算例替代核定作業計畫。","textEn":"Apply the following check at handover: Index delivered balance, neighbouring-hole responses and visible escape locations together. Link results to location, material batch and interpretation version. If large losses are credited as useful filling while high-permeability zones remain untreated, retain original records and obtain the responsible engineer's disposition; this example does not replace an approved work plan.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「幾何體積與實際注入量」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Geometric volume and delivered volume\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","將注入收支、相鄰孔反應及可見逸流位置共同索引。","泵表壓力永遠等於灌漿孔段實際壓力"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Index delivered balance, neighbouring-hole responses and visible escape locations together.","Pump-gauge pressure always equals actual pressure in the treated interval"],"answer":1,"explanation":"將注入收支、相鄰孔反應及可見逸流位置共同索引。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Index delivered balance, neighbouring-hole responses and visible escape locations together. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b163-v14-20","title":"幾何體積與實際注入量：失效診斷","titleEn":"Geometric volume and delivered volume: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b163-v14-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「幾何體積與實際注入量」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Geometric volume and delivered volume” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"大量外逸被當成有效填充，留下未處理的高滲區。相似表徵也可能由量測偏差造成，因此應回到將注入收支、相鄰孔反應及可見逸流位置共同索引，以獨立證據判別原因；只修補可見症狀將留下原本的傳力或滲流問題。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Large losses are credited as useful filling while high-permeability zones remain untreated. Similar symptoms can arise from measurement bias: return to index delivered balance, neighbouring-hole responses and visible escape locations together to discriminate the cause. Treating visible symptoms alone leaves the original transfer or seepage problem unresolved. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：判別這個機制時，應觀察將注入收支、相鄰孔反應及可見逸流位置共同索引；若出現大量外逸被當成有效填充，留下未處理的高滲區，便須重新檢查原先假設的接觸、力或水的傳遞邊界，而不能只調整計算結果。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: If large losses are credited as useful filling while high-permeability zones remain untreated, revisit the assumed contact, force or water-transfer boundary rather than merely adjusting the calculated result.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「注入量達理論體積就能證明處理半徑完全達成」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Delivered theoretical volume proves the complete treatment radius has been achieved\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b163-v14-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"大量外逸被當成有效填充，留下未處理的高滲區。相似表徵也可能由量測偏差造成，因此應回到將注入收支、相鄰孔反應及可見逸流位置共同索引，以獨立證據判別原因；只修補可見症狀將留下原本的傳力或滲流問題。","textEn":"Large losses are credited as useful filling while high-permeability zones remain untreated. Similar symptoms can arise from measurement bias: return to index delivered balance, neighbouring-hole responses and visible escape locations together to discriminate the cause. Treating visible symptoms alone leaves the original transfer or seepage problem unresolved.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"]},{"id":"b163-v14-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「幾何體積與實際注入量」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Geometric volume and delivered volume\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","入口壓力升高就能證明整個處理區都已封閉","大量外逸被當成有效填充，留下未處理的高滲區。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","Rising entrance pressure proves the entire treated zone is sealed","Large losses are credited as useful filling while high-permeability zones remain untreated."],"answer":2,"explanation":"大量外逸被當成有效填充，留下未處理的高滲區。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Large losses are credited as useful filling while high-permeability zones remain untreated. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b163-v14-21","title":"材料可灌性與粒徑：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Grout penetrability and particle size: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b163-v14-20"],"objective":"說明「材料可灌性與粒徑」如何影響高水壓隧道止水灌漿的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Grout penetrability and particle size” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Water-control grouting in high-pressure tunnels”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"材料能否進入裂隙取決於粒徑分布、開度、流變和過濾作用，平均粒徑不能代表最大團聚體。入口堵塞可能讓孔口壓力升高但深部仍未處理，因而壓力與流量變化不能直接解讀為地層已封閉；材料選擇需要相容試驗證據。 判別這個機制時，應觀察比較材料粒徑、濾失試驗與壓力流量曲線的形狀；若出現孔口濾餅造成假性拒漿，深部水路仍持續連通，便須重新檢查原先假設的接觸、力或水的傳遞邊界，而不能只調整計算結果。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「材料可灌性與粒徑」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Penetrability depends on size distribution, aperture, rheology and filtration, not mean particle size alone. Entrance clogging can raise collar pressure while leaving deeper ground untreated. Pressure-flow changes therefore do not directly establish closure and material selection needs compatibility evidence. Use the following check to discriminate the mechanism: Compare particle distribution, filtration tests and pressure-flow curve shapes. If an entrance filter cake produces apparent refusal while deeper pathways remain connected, revisit the assumed contact, force or water-transfer boundary rather than merely adjusting the calculated result. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Grout penetrability and particle size” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：geometricRatio=aperture/d95=0.20 mm/0.04 mm=5, not a universal penetrability criterion。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: geometricRatio=aperture/d95=0.20 mm/0.04 mm=5, not a universal penetrability criterion.","failure":"常見誤解：「入口壓力升高就能證明整個處理區都已封閉」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Rising entrance pressure proves the entire treated zone is sealed\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「材料可灌性與粒徑」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Grout penetrability and particle size”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b163-v14-21-k1","title":"材料可灌性與粒徑","titleEn":"Grout penetrability and particle size","text":"材料能否進入裂隙取決於粒徑分布、開度、流變和過濾作用，平均粒徑不能代表最大團聚體。入口堵塞可能讓孔口壓力升高但深部仍未處理，因而壓力與流量變化不能直接解讀為地層已封閉；材料選擇需要相容試驗證據。","textEn":"Penetrability depends on size distribution, aperture, rheology and filtration, not mean particle size alone. Entrance clogging can raise collar pressure while leaving deeper ground untreated.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"]},{"id":"b163-v14-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：入口壓力升高就能證明整個處理區都已封閉 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Rising entrance pressure proves the entire treated zone is sealed Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「材料可灌性與粒徑」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Grout penetrability and particle size\" is correct?","options":["材料能否進入裂隙取決於粒徑分布、開度、流變和過濾作用，平均粒徑不能代表最大團聚體。","入口壓力升高就能證明整個處理區都已封閉","處理後流量降低就一定全部來自灌漿改善"],"optionsEn":["Penetrability depends on size distribution, aperture, rheology and filtration, not mean particle size alone.","Rising entrance pressure proves the entire treated zone is sealed","Every post-treatment flow decrease is entirely caused by grouting improvement"],"answer":0,"explanation":"材料能否進入裂隙取決於粒徑分布、開度、流變和過濾作用，平均粒徑不能代表最大團聚體。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Penetrability depends on size distribution, aperture, rheology and filtration, not mean particle size alone. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b163-v14-22","title":"材料可灌性與粒徑：定量估算","titleEn":"Grout penetrability and particle size: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b163-v14-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「材料可灌性與粒徑」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Grout penetrability and particle size” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：geometricRatio=aperture/d95=0.20 mm/0.04 mm=5, not a universal penetrability criterion。算例只描述水力關係，不提供現地配方、注入壓力或施作授權。 此結果僅用來核對量綱及模型敏感度，不是專案設計值、實測紀錄或現場允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: geometricRatio=aperture/d95=0.20 mm/0.04 mm=5, not a universal penetrability criterion. Examples describe hydraulic relationships, not field recipes, injection pressures or operating authorization. This checks dimensions and model sensitivity; it is neither measured project data nor a design or acceptance value. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：比較材料粒徑、濾失試驗與壓力流量曲線的形狀。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare particle distribution, filtration tests and pressure-flow curve shapes.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b163-v14-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：geometricRatio=aperture/d95=0.20 mm/0.04 mm=5, not a universal penetrability criterion。算例只描述水力關係，不提供現地配方、注入壓力或施作授權。 此結果僅用來核對量綱及模型敏感度，不是專案設計值、實測紀錄或現場允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: geometricRatio=aperture/d95=0.20 mm/0.04 mm=5, not a universal penetrability criterion. Examples describe hydraulic relationships, not field recipes, injection pressures or operating authorization. This checks dimensions and model sensitivity; it is neither measured project data nor a design or acceptance value.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"]},{"id":"b163-v14-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「材料可灌性與粒徑」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Grout penetrability and particle size\", which statement holds?","options":["施工後短期不漏就代表材料永遠不會劣化","原創教學假設：geometricRatio=aperture/d95=0.20 mm/0.04 mm=5, not a universal penetrability criterion。","隧道埋得多深就一定有完全相同的地下水頭"],"optionsEn":["Initial absence of leakage proves the material will never deteriorate","Original teaching assumptions: geometricRatio=aperture/d95=0.20 mm/0.04 mm=5, not a universal penetrability criterion.","Tunnel burial depth always equals the groundwater head"],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：geometricRatio=aperture/d95=0.20 mm/0.04 mm=5, not a universal penetrability criterion。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: geometricRatio=aperture/d95=0.20 mm/0.04 mm=5, not a universal penetrability criterion. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b163-v14-23","title":"材料可灌性與粒徑：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Grout penetrability and particle size: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b163-v14-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「材料可灌性與粒徑」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Grout penetrability and particle size” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"比較材料粒徑、濾失試驗與壓力流量曲線的形狀。量測須保存位置、時間及基準，讓同條件的重複結果可比較；並特別檢查「孔口濾餅造成假性拒漿，深部水路仍持續連通」是否能由這組資料區分。儀器校核與誤差估計應先於判讀，由負責技師核定該項試驗的允收和停留點。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare particle distribution, filtration tests and pressure-flow curve shapes. Retain position, time and datums for comparable repeats, specifically distinguishing this scenario: An entrance filter cake produces apparent refusal while deeper pathways remain connected. Instrument checks and uncertainty estimates precede interpretation; the responsible engineer sets acceptance and hold points for this test. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將比較材料粒徑、濾失試驗與壓力流量曲線的形狀列為該構件的交接證據，連結到施工位置、材料批次及判讀版本。若發現孔口濾餅造成假性拒漿，深部水路仍持續連通，先保留原始紀錄並由負責技師確認處置，不能以本課算例替代核定作業計畫。","observationEn":"Site practice: Apply the following check at handover: Compare particle distribution, filtration tests and pressure-flow curve shapes. Link results to location, material batch and interpretation version. If an entrance filter cake produces apparent refusal while deeper pathways remain connected, retain original records and obtain the responsible engineer's disposition; this example does not replace an approved work plan.","failure":"注意干擾：孔口濾餅造成假性拒漿，深部水路仍持續連通。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: An entrance filter cake produces apparent refusal while deeper pathways remain connected. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b163-v14-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"比較材料粒徑、濾失試驗與壓力流量曲線的形狀。量測須保存位置、時間及基準，讓同條件的重複結果可比較；並特別檢查「孔口濾餅造成假性拒漿，深部水路仍持續連通」是否能由這組資料區分。儀器校核與誤差估計應先於判讀，由負責技師核定該項試驗的允收和停留點。","textEn":"Compare particle distribution, filtration tests and pressure-flow curve shapes. Retain position, time and datums for comparable repeats, specifically distinguishing this scenario: An entrance filter cake produces apparent refusal while deeper pathways remain connected. Instrument checks and uncertainty estimates precede interpretation; the responsible engineer sets acceptance and hold points for this test.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"]},{"id":"b163-v14-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將比較材料粒徑、濾失試驗與壓力流量曲線的形狀列為該構件的交接證據，連結到施工位置、材料批次及判讀版本。若發現孔口濾餅造成假性拒漿，深部水路仍持續連通，先保留原始紀錄並由負責技師確認處置，不能以本課算例替代核定作業計畫。","textEn":"Apply the following check at handover: Compare particle distribution, filtration tests and pressure-flow curve shapes. Link results to location, material batch and interpretation version. If an entrance filter cake produces apparent refusal while deeper pathways remain connected, retain original records and obtain the responsible engineer's disposition; this example does not replace an approved work plan.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「材料可灌性與粒徑」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Grout penetrability and particle size\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","淨注入壓差低就能保證任何地層都不會開裂","比較材料粒徑、濾失試驗與壓力流量曲線的形狀。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","A low net injection difference guarantees no ground can fracture","Compare particle distribution, filtration tests and pressure-flow curve shapes."],"answer":2,"explanation":"比較材料粒徑、濾失試驗與壓力流量曲線的形狀。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare particle distribution, filtration tests and pressure-flow curve shapes. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b163-v14-24","title":"材料可灌性與粒徑：失效診斷","titleEn":"Grout penetrability and particle size: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b163-v14-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「材料可灌性與粒徑」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Grout penetrability and particle size” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"孔口濾餅造成假性拒漿，深部水路仍持續連通。相似表徵也可能由量測偏差造成，因此應回到比較材料粒徑、濾失試驗與壓力流量曲線的形狀，以獨立證據判別原因；只修補可見症狀將留下原本的傳力或滲流問題。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"An entrance filter cake produces apparent refusal while deeper pathways remain connected. Similar symptoms can arise from measurement bias: return to compare particle distribution, filtration tests and pressure-flow curve shapes to discriminate the cause. Treating visible symptoms alone leaves the original transfer or seepage problem unresolved. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：判別這個機制時，應觀察比較材料粒徑、濾失試驗與壓力流量曲線的形狀；若出現孔口濾餅造成假性拒漿，深部水路仍持續連通，便須重新檢查原先假設的接觸、力或水的傳遞邊界，而不能只調整計算結果。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: If an entrance filter cake produces apparent refusal while deeper pathways remain connected, revisit the assumed contact, force or water-transfer boundary rather than merely adjusting the calculated result.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「入口壓力升高就能證明整個處理區都已封閉」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Rising entrance pressure proves the entire treated zone is sealed\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b163-v14-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"孔口濾餅造成假性拒漿，深部水路仍持續連通。相似表徵也可能由量測偏差造成，因此應回到比較材料粒徑、濾失試驗與壓力流量曲線的形狀，以獨立證據判別原因；只修補可見症狀將留下原本的傳力或滲流問題。","textEn":"An entrance filter cake produces apparent refusal while deeper pathways remain connected. Similar symptoms can arise from measurement bias: return to compare particle distribution, filtration tests and pressure-flow curve shapes to discriminate the cause. Treating visible symptoms alone leaves the original transfer or seepage problem unresolved.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"]},{"id":"b163-v14-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「材料可灌性與粒徑」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Grout penetrability and particle size\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["孔口濾餅造成假性拒漿，深部水路仍持續連通。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","處理後流量降低就一定全部來自灌漿改善"],"optionsEn":["An entrance filter cake produces apparent refusal while deeper pathways remain connected.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","Every post-treatment flow decrease is entirely caused by grouting improvement"],"answer":0,"explanation":"孔口濾餅造成假性拒漿，深部水路仍持續連通。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"An entrance filter cake produces apparent refusal while deeper pathways remain connected. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b163-v14-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「前後透水比較與水頭」與「地層抬升與遠端反應」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Before-after permeability and head\" and \"Ground uplift and remote response\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b163-v14-25","title":"前後透水比較與水頭：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Before-after permeability and head: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b163-v14-24"],"objective":"說明「前後透水比較與水頭」如何影響高水壓隧道止水灌漿的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Before-after permeability and head” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Water-control grouting in high-pressure tunnels”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"處理前後流量若在不同水頭下量測，直接百分比可能混入地下水自然變化。線性水力導通度只適用特定範圍，裂隙開合會造成非線性；比較應使用相同孔段、時間尺度及可比邊界，並保留未達穩態的資料註記。 判別這個機制時，應觀察在相同孔段和可比水頭下比較穩態流量及恢復曲線；若出現天然水位下降被錯算成灌漿成效，雨季水頭恢復後再漏，便須重新檢查原先假設的接觸、力或水的傳遞邊界，而不能只調整計算結果。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「前後透水比較與水頭」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Before-after flows measured at different heads mix treatment with natural groundwater change. Linear conductance applies only over a specified range because joint opening can be nonlinear. Compare the same intervals and time scales under similar boundaries and identify readings that have not reached steady conditions. Use the following check to discriminate the mechanism: Compare steady flow and recovery curves in matching intervals at comparable heads. If natural head decline is credited to treatment and leakage returns when seasonal head recovers, revisit the assumed contact, force or water-transfer boundary rather than merely adjusting the calculated result. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Before-after permeability and head” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：reduction=(Qbefore-Qafter)/Qbefore=(10-2) L/min/10 L/min=80 percent at equal head。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: reduction=(Qbefore-Qafter)/Qbefore=(10-2) L/min/10 L/min=80 percent at equal head.","failure":"常見誤解：「處理後流量降低就一定全部來自灌漿改善」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Every post-treatment flow decrease is entirely caused by grouting improvement\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「前後透水比較與水頭」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Before-after permeability and head”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b163-v14-25-k1","title":"前後透水比較與水頭","titleEn":"Before-after permeability and head","text":"處理前後流量若在不同水頭下量測，直接百分比可能混入地下水自然變化。線性水力導通度只適用特定範圍，裂隙開合會造成非線性；比較應使用相同孔段、時間尺度及可比邊界，並保留未達穩態的資料註記。","textEn":"Before-after flows measured at different heads mix treatment with natural groundwater change. Linear conductance applies only over a specified range because joint opening can be nonlinear.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"]},{"id":"b163-v14-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：處理後流量降低就一定全部來自灌漿改善 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Every post-treatment flow decrease is entirely caused by grouting improvement Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「前後透水比較與水頭」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Before-after permeability and head\" is correct?","options":["處理後流量降低就一定全部來自灌漿改善","處理前後流量若在不同水頭下量測，直接百分比可能混入地下水自然變化。","孔口周圍沒變形就能證明所有遠端地層都沒反應"],"optionsEn":["Every post-treatment flow decrease is entirely caused by grouting improvement","Before-after flows measured at different heads mix treatment with natural groundwater change.","No movement near the collar proves all distant ground remains unaffected"],"answer":1,"explanation":"處理前後流量若在不同水頭下量測，直接百分比可能混入地下水自然變化。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Before-after flows measured at different heads mix treatment with natural groundwater change. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b163-v14-26","title":"前後透水比較與水頭：定量估算","titleEn":"Before-after permeability and head: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b163-v14-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「前後透水比較與水頭」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Before-after permeability and head” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：reduction=(Qbefore-Qafter)/Qbefore=(10-2) L/min/10 L/min=80 percent at equal head。算例只描述水力關係，不提供現地配方、注入壓力或施作授權。 此結果僅用來核對量綱及模型敏感度，不是專案設計值、實測紀錄或現場允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: reduction=(Qbefore-Qafter)/Qbefore=(10-2) L/min/10 L/min=80 percent at equal head. Examples describe hydraulic relationships, not field recipes, injection pressures or operating authorization. This checks dimensions and model sensitivity; it is neither measured project data nor a design or acceptance value. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在相同孔段和可比水頭下比較穩態流量及恢復曲線。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare steady flow and recovery curves in matching intervals at comparable heads.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b163-v14-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：reduction=(Qbefore-Qafter)/Qbefore=(10-2) L/min/10 L/min=80 percent at equal head。算例只描述水力關係，不提供現地配方、注入壓力或施作授權。 此結果僅用來核對量綱及模型敏感度，不是專案設計值、實測紀錄或現場允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: reduction=(Qbefore-Qafter)/Qbefore=(10-2) L/min/10 L/min=80 percent at equal head. Examples describe hydraulic relationships, not field recipes, injection pressures or operating authorization. This checks dimensions and model sensitivity; it is neither measured project data nor a design or acceptance value.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"]},{"id":"b163-v14-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「前後透水比較與水頭」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Before-after permeability and head\", which statement holds?","options":["中心驗證孔合格就能代表整個止水範圍連續","泵表壓力永遠等於灌漿孔段實際壓力","原創教學假設：reduction=(Qbefore-Qafter)/Qbefore=(10-2) L/min/10 L/min=80 percent at equal head。"],"optionsEn":["A passing central verification hole proves the entire water barrier is continuous","Pump-gauge pressure always equals actual pressure in the treated interval","Original teaching assumptions: reduction=(Qbefore-Qafter)/Qbefore=(10-2) L/min/10 L/min=80 percent at equal head."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：reduction=(Qbefore-Qafter)/Qbefore=(10-2) L/min/10 L/min=80 percent at equal head。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: reduction=(Qbefore-Qafter)/Qbefore=(10-2) L/min/10 L/min=80 percent at equal head. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b163-v14-27","title":"前後透水比較與水頭：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Before-after permeability and head: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b163-v14-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「前後透水比較與水頭」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Before-after permeability and head” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在相同孔段和可比水頭下比較穩態流量及恢復曲線。量測須保存位置、時間及基準，讓同條件的重複結果可比較；並特別檢查「天然水位下降被錯算成灌漿成效，雨季水頭恢復後再漏」是否能由這組資料區分。儀器校核與誤差估計應先於判讀，由負責技師核定該項試驗的允收和停留點。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare steady flow and recovery curves in matching intervals at comparable heads. Retain position, time and datums for comparable repeats, specifically distinguishing this scenario: Natural head decline is credited to treatment and leakage returns when seasonal head recovers. Instrument checks and uncertainty estimates precede interpretation; the responsible engineer sets acceptance and hold points for this test. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將在相同孔段和可比水頭下比較穩態流量及恢復曲線列為該構件的交接證據，連結到施工位置、材料批次及判讀版本。若發現天然水位下降被錯算成灌漿成效，雨季水頭恢復後再漏，先保留原始紀錄並由負責技師確認處置，不能以本課算例替代核定作業計畫。","observationEn":"Site practice: Apply the following check at handover: Compare steady flow and recovery curves in matching intervals at comparable heads. Link results to location, material batch and interpretation version. If natural head decline is credited to treatment and leakage returns when seasonal head recovers, retain original records and obtain the responsible engineer's disposition; this example does not replace an approved work plan.","failure":"注意干擾：天然水位下降被錯算成灌漿成效，雨季水頭恢復後再漏。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Natural head decline is credited to treatment and leakage returns when seasonal head recovers. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b163-v14-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在相同孔段和可比水頭下比較穩態流量及恢復曲線。量測須保存位置、時間及基準，讓同條件的重複結果可比較；並特別檢查「天然水位下降被錯算成灌漿成效，雨季水頭恢復後再漏」是否能由這組資料區分。儀器校核與誤差估計應先於判讀，由負責技師核定該項試驗的允收和停留點。","textEn":"Compare steady flow and recovery curves in matching intervals at comparable heads. Retain position, time and datums for comparable repeats, specifically distinguishing this scenario: Natural head decline is credited to treatment and leakage returns when seasonal head recovers. Instrument checks and uncertainty estimates precede interpretation; the responsible engineer sets acceptance and hold points for this test.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"]},{"id":"b163-v14-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將在相同孔段和可比水頭下比較穩態流量及恢復曲線列為該構件的交接證據，連結到施工位置、材料批次及判讀版本。若發現天然水位下降被錯算成灌漿成效，雨季水頭恢復後再漏，先保留原始紀錄並由負責技師確認處置，不能以本課算例替代核定作業計畫。","textEn":"Apply the following check at handover: Compare steady flow and recovery curves in matching intervals at comparable heads. Link results to location, material batch and interpretation version. If natural head decline is credited to treatment and leakage returns when seasonal head recovers, retain original records and obtain the responsible engineer's disposition; this example does not replace an approved work plan.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「前後透水比較與水頭」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Before-after permeability and head\"?","options":["在相同孔段和可比水頭下比較穩態流量及恢復曲線。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、開挖序列與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","所有裂隙對總漏水的貢獻都大致相同"],"optionsEn":["Compare steady flow and recovery curves in matching intervals at comparable heads.","Temperature, water head, excavation sequence and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Every fracture contributes approximately equally to total leakage"],"answer":0,"explanation":"在相同孔段和可比水頭下比較穩態流量及恢復曲線。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare steady flow and recovery curves in matching intervals at comparable heads. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b163-v14-28","title":"前後透水比較與水頭：失效診斷","titleEn":"Before-after permeability and head: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b163-v14-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「前後透水比較與水頭」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Before-after permeability and head” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"天然水位下降被錯算成灌漿成效，雨季水頭恢復後再漏。相似表徵也可能由量測偏差造成，因此應回到在相同孔段和可比水頭下比較穩態流量及恢復曲線，以獨立證據判別原因；只修補可見症狀將留下原本的傳力或滲流問題。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Natural head decline is credited to treatment and leakage returns when seasonal head recovers. Similar symptoms can arise from measurement bias: return to compare steady flow and recovery curves in matching intervals at comparable heads to discriminate the cause. Treating visible symptoms alone leaves the original transfer or seepage problem unresolved. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：判別這個機制時，應觀察在相同孔段和可比水頭下比較穩態流量及恢復曲線；若出現天然水位下降被錯算成灌漿成效，雨季水頭恢復後再漏，便須重新檢查原先假設的接觸、力或水的傳遞邊界，而不能只調整計算結果。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: If natural head decline is credited to treatment and leakage returns when seasonal head recovers, revisit the assumed contact, force or water-transfer boundary rather than merely adjusting the calculated result.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「處理後流量降低就一定全部來自灌漿改善」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Every post-treatment flow decrease is entirely caused by grouting improvement\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b163-v14-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"天然水位下降被錯算成灌漿成效，雨季水頭恢復後再漏。相似表徵也可能由量測偏差造成，因此應回到在相同孔段和可比水頭下比較穩態流量及恢復曲線，以獨立證據判別原因；只修補可見症狀將留下原本的傳力或滲流問題。","textEn":"Natural head decline is credited to treatment and leakage returns when seasonal head recovers. Similar symptoms can arise from measurement bias: return to compare steady flow and recovery curves in matching intervals at comparable heads to discriminate the cause. Treating visible symptoms alone leaves the original transfer or seepage problem unresolved.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"]},{"id":"b163-v14-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「前後透水比較與水頭」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Before-after permeability and head\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","天然水位下降被錯算成灌漿成效，雨季水頭恢復後再漏。","孔口周圍沒變形就能證明所有遠端地層都沒反應"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Natural head decline is credited to treatment and leakage returns when seasonal head recovers.","No movement near the collar proves all distant ground remains unaffected"],"answer":1,"explanation":"天然水位下降被錯算成灌漿成效，雨季水頭恢復後再漏。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Natural head decline is credited to treatment and leakage returns when seasonal head recovers. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b163-v14-29","title":"地層抬升與遠端反應：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Ground uplift and remote response: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b163-v14-28"],"objective":"說明「地層抬升與遠端反應」如何影響高水壓隧道止水灌漿的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Ground uplift and remote response” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Water-control grouting in high-pressure tunnels”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"壓力傳遞可能超出預期處理半徑，薄弱界面或地表覆土較少處會先變形。孔口附近沒有移動不能排除遠端反應，鄰近結構與水位也可能提供訊息；監測範圍應由地質連通模型決定，而不是固定圍住設備。 判別這個機制時，應觀察將地表水準、結構位移和相鄰孔壓放在共同時間軸；若出現遠端抬升先發生卻未佈點，局部監測誤判沒有影響，便須重新檢查原先假設的接觸、力或水的傳遞邊界，而不能只調整計算結果。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「地層抬升與遠端反應」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Pressure transmission can extend beyond the assumed treatment radius and deform weak or shallow interfaces first. No collar movement does not exclude remote response; nearby structures and heads supply additional evidence. Base monitoring coverage on geological connectivity rather than a fixed circle around equipment. Use the following check to discriminate the mechanism: Align surface levels, structural movement and neighbouring pore pressures. If uninstrumented remote uplift begins while local monitoring falsely suggests no effect, revisit the assumed contact, force or water-transfer boundary rather than merely adjusting the calculated result. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Ground uplift and remote response” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：upliftGradient=levelDifference/distance=2 mm/10 m=0.0002。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: upliftGradient=levelDifference/distance=2 mm/10 m=0.0002.","failure":"常見誤解：「孔口周圍沒變形就能證明所有遠端地層都沒反應」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"No movement near the collar proves all distant ground remains unaffected\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「地層抬升與遠端反應」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Ground uplift and remote response”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b163-v14-29-k1","title":"地層抬升與遠端反應","titleEn":"Ground uplift and remote response","text":"壓力傳遞可能超出預期處理半徑，薄弱界面或地表覆土較少處會先變形。孔口附近沒有移動不能排除遠端反應，鄰近結構與水位也可能提供訊息；監測範圍應由地質連通模型決定，而不是固定圍住設備。","textEn":"Pressure transmission can extend beyond the assumed treatment radius and deform weak or shallow interfaces first. No collar movement does not exclude remote response; nearby structures and heads supply additional evidence.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"]},{"id":"b163-v14-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：孔口周圍沒變形就能證明所有遠端地層都沒反應 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: No movement near the collar proves all distant ground remains unaffected Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「地層抬升與遠端反應」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Ground uplift and remote response\" is correct?","options":["孔口周圍沒變形就能證明所有遠端地層都沒反應","施工後短期不漏就代表材料永遠不會劣化","壓力傳遞可能超出預期處理半徑，薄弱界面或地表覆土較少處會先變形。"],"optionsEn":["No movement near the collar proves all distant ground remains unaffected","Initial absence of leakage proves the material will never deteriorate","Pressure transmission can extend beyond the assumed treatment radius and deform weak or shallow interfaces first."],"answer":2,"explanation":"壓力傳遞可能超出預期處理半徑，薄弱界面或地表覆土較少處會先變形。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Pressure transmission can extend beyond the assumed treatment radius and deform weak or shallow interfaces first. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b163-v14-30","title":"地層抬升與遠端反應：定量估算","titleEn":"Ground uplift and remote response: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b163-v14-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「地層抬升與遠端反應」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Ground uplift and remote response” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：upliftGradient=levelDifference/distance=2 mm/10 m=0.0002。算例只描述水力關係，不提供現地配方、注入壓力或施作授權。 此結果僅用來核對量綱及模型敏感度，不是專案設計值、實測紀錄或現場允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: upliftGradient=levelDifference/distance=2 mm/10 m=0.0002. Examples describe hydraulic relationships, not field recipes, injection pressures or operating authorization. This checks dimensions and model sensitivity; it is neither measured project data nor a design or acceptance value. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將地表水準、結構位移和相鄰孔壓放在共同時間軸。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Align surface levels, structural movement and neighbouring pore pressures.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b163-v14-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：upliftGradient=levelDifference/distance=2 mm/10 m=0.0002。算例只描述水力關係，不提供現地配方、注入壓力或施作授權。 此結果僅用來核對量綱及模型敏感度，不是專案設計值、實測紀錄或現場允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: upliftGradient=levelDifference/distance=2 mm/10 m=0.0002. Examples describe hydraulic relationships, not field recipes, injection pressures or operating authorization. This checks dimensions and model sensitivity; it is neither measured project data nor a design or acceptance value.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"]},{"id":"b163-v14-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「地層抬升與遠端反應」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Ground uplift and remote response\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：upliftGradient=levelDifference/distance=2 mm/10 m=0.0002。","隧道埋得多深就一定有完全相同的地下水頭","淨注入壓差低就能保證任何地層都不會開裂"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: upliftGradient=levelDifference/distance=2 mm/10 m=0.0002.","Tunnel burial depth always equals the groundwater head","A low net injection difference guarantees no ground can fracture"],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：upliftGradient=levelDifference/distance=2 mm/10 m=0.0002。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: upliftGradient=levelDifference/distance=2 mm/10 m=0.0002. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b163-v14-31","title":"地層抬升與遠端反應：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Ground uplift and remote response: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b163-v14-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「地層抬升與遠端反應」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Ground uplift and remote response” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將地表水準、結構位移和相鄰孔壓放在共同時間軸。量測須保存位置、時間及基準，讓同條件的重複結果可比較；並特別檢查「遠端抬升先發生卻未佈點，局部監測誤判沒有影響」是否能由這組資料區分。儀器校核與誤差估計應先於判讀，由負責技師核定該項試驗的允收和停留點。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Align surface levels, structural movement and neighbouring pore pressures. Retain position, time and datums for comparable repeats, specifically distinguishing this scenario: Uninstrumented remote uplift begins while local monitoring falsely suggests no effect. Instrument checks and uncertainty estimates precede interpretation; the responsible engineer sets acceptance and hold points for this test. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將將地表水準、結構位移和相鄰孔壓放在共同時間軸列為該構件的交接證據，連結到施工位置、材料批次及判讀版本。若發現遠端抬升先發生卻未佈點，局部監測誤判沒有影響，先保留原始紀錄並由負責技師確認處置，不能以本課算例替代核定作業計畫。","observationEn":"Site practice: Apply the following check at handover: Align surface levels, structural movement and neighbouring pore pressures. Link results to location, material batch and interpretation version. If uninstrumented remote uplift begins while local monitoring falsely suggests no effect, retain original records and obtain the responsible engineer's disposition; this example does not replace an approved work plan.","failure":"注意干擾：遠端抬升先發生卻未佈點，局部監測誤判沒有影響。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Uninstrumented remote uplift begins while local monitoring falsely suggests no effect. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b163-v14-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將地表水準、結構位移和相鄰孔壓放在共同時間軸。量測須保存位置、時間及基準，讓同條件的重複結果可比較；並特別檢查「遠端抬升先發生卻未佈點，局部監測誤判沒有影響」是否能由這組資料區分。儀器校核與誤差估計應先於判讀，由負責技師核定該項試驗的允收和停留點。","textEn":"Align surface levels, structural movement and neighbouring pore pressures. Retain position, time and datums for comparable repeats, specifically distinguishing this scenario: Uninstrumented remote uplift begins while local monitoring falsely suggests no effect. Instrument checks and uncertainty estimates precede interpretation; the responsible engineer sets acceptance and hold points for this test.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"]},{"id":"b163-v14-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將將地表水準、結構位移和相鄰孔壓放在共同時間軸列為該構件的交接證據，連結到施工位置、材料批次及判讀版本。若發現遠端抬升先發生卻未佈點，局部監測誤判沒有影響，先保留原始紀錄並由負責技師確認處置，不能以本課算例替代核定作業計畫。","textEn":"Apply the following check at handover: Align surface levels, structural movement and neighbouring pore pressures. Link results to location, material batch and interpretation version. If uninstrumented remote uplift begins while local monitoring falsely suggests no effect, retain original records and obtain the responsible engineer's disposition; this example does not replace an approved work plan.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「地層抬升與遠端反應」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Ground uplift and remote response\"?","options":["沿用另一條隧道或另一處地層的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","將地表水準、結構位移和相鄰孔壓放在共同時間軸。","注入量達理論體積就能證明處理半徑完全達成"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another tunnel or ground formation counts as verifying this structure.","Align surface levels, structural movement and neighbouring pore pressures.","Delivered theoretical volume proves the complete treatment radius has been achieved"],"answer":1,"explanation":"將地表水準、結構位移和相鄰孔壓放在共同時間軸。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Align surface levels, structural movement and neighbouring pore pressures. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b163-v14-32","title":"地層抬升與遠端反應：失效診斷","titleEn":"Ground uplift and remote response: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b163-v14-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「地層抬升與遠端反應」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Ground uplift and remote response” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"遠端抬升先發生卻未佈點，局部監測誤判沒有影響。相似表徵也可能由量測偏差造成，因此應回到將地表水準、結構位移和相鄰孔壓放在共同時間軸，以獨立證據判別原因；只修補可見症狀將留下原本的傳力或滲流問題。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Uninstrumented remote uplift begins while local monitoring falsely suggests no effect. Similar symptoms can arise from measurement bias: return to align surface levels, structural movement and neighbouring pore pressures to discriminate the cause. Treating visible symptoms alone leaves the original transfer or seepage problem unresolved. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：判別這個機制時，應觀察將地表水準、結構位移和相鄰孔壓放在共同時間軸；若出現遠端抬升先發生卻未佈點，局部監測誤判沒有影響，便須重新檢查原先假設的接觸、力或水的傳遞邊界，而不能只調整計算結果。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: If uninstrumented remote uplift begins while local monitoring falsely suggests no effect, revisit the assumed contact, force or water-transfer boundary rather than merely adjusting the calculated result.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「孔口周圍沒變形就能證明所有遠端地層都沒反應」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"No movement near the collar proves all distant ground remains unaffected\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b163-v14-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"遠端抬升先發生卻未佈點，局部監測誤判沒有影響。相似表徵也可能由量測偏差造成，因此應回到將地表水準、結構位移和相鄰孔壓放在共同時間軸，以獨立證據判別原因；只修補可見症狀將留下原本的傳力或滲流問題。","textEn":"Uninstrumented remote uplift begins while local monitoring falsely suggests no effect. Similar symptoms can arise from measurement bias: return to align surface levels, structural movement and neighbouring pore pressures to discriminate the cause. Treating visible symptoms alone leaves the original transfer or seepage problem unresolved.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"]},{"id":"b163-v14-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「地層抬升與遠端反應」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Ground uplift and remote response\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","施工後短期不漏就代表材料永遠不會劣化","遠端抬升先發生卻未佈點，局部監測誤判沒有影響。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Initial absence of leakage proves the material will never deteriorate","Uninstrumented remote uplift begins while local monitoring falsely suggests no effect."],"answer":2,"explanation":"遠端抬升先發生卻未佈點，局部監測誤判沒有影響。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Uninstrumented remote uplift begins while local monitoring falsely suggests no effect. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b163-v14-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「水化學與耐久相容」與「驗收範圍與長期水路」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Water chemistry and durability compatibility\" and \"Acceptance coverage and long-term pathways\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b163-v14-33","title":"水化學與耐久相容：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Water chemistry and durability compatibility: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b163-v14-32"],"objective":"說明「水化學與耐久相容」如何影響高水壓隧道止水灌漿的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Water chemistry and durability compatibility” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Water-control grouting in high-pressure tunnels”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"止水材料長期接觸地下水，化學侵蝕、溶出或體積變化可能改變密封效果。短期不漏不等於材料與環境相容，溫度和流速也影響暴露；試驗應比較服務環境下的留存性能，而非只採容易得到的室內浸泡結果。 判別這個機制時，應觀察將水質、溫度及老化後滲透與強度資料共同審查；若出現材料溶出留下新通道，短期合格卻長期重新滲漏，便須重新檢查原先假設的接觸、力或水的傳遞邊界，而不能只調整計算結果。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「水化學與耐久相容」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Water-control materials remain exposed to groundwater, where attack, leaching and volume change can alter sealing. Initial tightness does not establish compatibility, and temperature and flow affect exposure. Compare retained performance under representative service conditions rather than convenient immersion results alone. Use the following check to discriminate the mechanism: Review water chemistry, temperature and post-ageing permeability and strength together. If material leaching creates new pathways despite initially passing leakage checks, revisit the assumed contact, force or water-transfer boundary rather than merely adjusting the calculated result. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Water chemistry and durability compatibility” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：retainedStrength=aged/reference=8 MPa/10 MPa=80 percent。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: retainedStrength=aged/reference=8 MPa/10 MPa=80 percent.","failure":"常見誤解：「施工後短期不漏就代表材料永遠不會劣化」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Initial absence of leakage proves the material will never deteriorate\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「水化學與耐久相容」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Water chemistry and durability compatibility”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b163-v14-33-k1","title":"水化學與耐久相容","titleEn":"Water chemistry and durability compatibility","text":"止水材料長期接觸地下水，化學侵蝕、溶出或體積變化可能改變密封效果。短期不漏不等於材料與環境相容，溫度和流速也影響暴露；試驗應比較服務環境下的留存性能，而非只採容易得到的室內浸泡結果。","textEn":"Water-control materials remain exposed to groundwater, where attack, leaching and volume change can alter sealing. Initial tightness does not establish compatibility, and temperature and flow affect exposure.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"]},{"id":"b163-v14-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：施工後短期不漏就代表材料永遠不會劣化 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Initial absence of leakage proves the material will never deteriorate Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「水化學與耐久相容」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Water chemistry and durability compatibility\" is correct?","options":["止水材料長期接觸地下水，化學侵蝕、溶出或體積變化可能改變密封效果。","施工後短期不漏就代表材料永遠不會劣化","中心驗證孔合格就能代表整個止水範圍連續"],"optionsEn":["Water-control materials remain exposed to groundwater, where attack, leaching and volume change can alter sealing.","Initial absence of leakage proves the material will never deteriorate","A passing central verification hole proves the entire water barrier is continuous"],"answer":0,"explanation":"止水材料長期接觸地下水，化學侵蝕、溶出或體積變化可能改變密封效果。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Water-control materials remain exposed to groundwater, where attack, leaching and volume change can alter sealing. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b163-v14-34","title":"水化學與耐久相容：定量估算","titleEn":"Water chemistry and durability compatibility: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b163-v14-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「水化學與耐久相容」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Water chemistry and durability compatibility” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：retainedStrength=aged/reference=8 MPa/10 MPa=80 percent。算例只描述水力關係，不提供現地配方、注入壓力或施作授權。 此結果僅用來核對量綱及模型敏感度，不是專案設計值、實測紀錄或現場允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: retainedStrength=aged/reference=8 MPa/10 MPa=80 percent. Examples describe hydraulic relationships, not field recipes, injection pressures or operating authorization. This checks dimensions and model sensitivity; it is neither measured project data nor a design or acceptance value. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將水質、溫度及老化後滲透與強度資料共同審查。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Review water chemistry, temperature and post-ageing permeability and strength together.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b163-v14-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：retainedStrength=aged/reference=8 MPa/10 MPa=80 percent。算例只描述水力關係，不提供現地配方、注入壓力或施作授權。 此結果僅用來核對量綱及模型敏感度，不是專案設計值、實測紀錄或現場允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: retainedStrength=aged/reference=8 MPa/10 MPa=80 percent. Examples describe hydraulic relationships, not field recipes, injection pressures or operating authorization. This checks dimensions and model sensitivity; it is neither measured project data nor a design or acceptance value.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"]},{"id":"b163-v14-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「水化學與耐久相容」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Water chemistry and durability compatibility\", which statement holds?","options":["泵表壓力永遠等於灌漿孔段實際壓力","原創教學假設：retainedStrength=aged/reference=8 MPa/10 MPa=80 percent。","所有裂隙對總漏水的貢獻都大致相同"],"optionsEn":["Pump-gauge pressure always equals actual pressure in the treated interval","Original teaching assumptions: retainedStrength=aged/reference=8 MPa/10 MPa=80 percent.","Every fracture contributes approximately equally to total leakage"],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：retainedStrength=aged/reference=8 MPa/10 MPa=80 percent。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: retainedStrength=aged/reference=8 MPa/10 MPa=80 percent. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b163-v14-35","title":"水化學與耐久相容：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Water chemistry and durability compatibility: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b163-v14-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「水化學與耐久相容」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Water chemistry and durability compatibility” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將水質、溫度及老化後滲透與強度資料共同審查。量測須保存位置、時間及基準，讓同條件的重複結果可比較；並特別檢查「材料溶出留下新通道，短期合格卻長期重新滲漏」是否能由這組資料區分。儀器校核與誤差估計應先於判讀，由負責技師核定該項試驗的允收和停留點。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Review water chemistry, temperature and post-ageing permeability and strength together. Retain position, time and datums for comparable repeats, specifically distinguishing this scenario: Material leaching creates new pathways despite initially passing leakage checks. Instrument checks and uncertainty estimates precede interpretation; the responsible engineer sets acceptance and hold points for this test. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將將水質、溫度及老化後滲透與強度資料共同審查列為該構件的交接證據，連結到施工位置、材料批次及判讀版本。若發現材料溶出留下新通道，短期合格卻長期重新滲漏，先保留原始紀錄並由負責技師確認處置，不能以本課算例替代核定作業計畫。","observationEn":"Site practice: Apply the following check at handover: Review water chemistry, temperature and post-ageing permeability and strength together. Link results to location, material batch and interpretation version. If material leaching creates new pathways despite initially passing leakage checks, retain original records and obtain the responsible engineer's disposition; this example does not replace an approved work plan.","failure":"注意干擾：材料溶出留下新通道，短期合格卻長期重新滲漏。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Material leaching creates new pathways despite initially passing leakage checks. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b163-v14-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將水質、溫度及老化後滲透與強度資料共同審查。量測須保存位置、時間及基準，讓同條件的重複結果可比較；並特別檢查「材料溶出留下新通道，短期合格卻長期重新滲漏」是否能由這組資料區分。儀器校核與誤差估計應先於判讀，由負責技師核定該項試驗的允收和停留點。","textEn":"Review water chemistry, temperature and post-ageing permeability and strength together. Retain position, time and datums for comparable repeats, specifically distinguishing this scenario: Material leaching creates new pathways despite initially passing leakage checks. Instrument checks and uncertainty estimates precede interpretation; the responsible engineer sets acceptance and hold points for this test.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"]},{"id":"b163-v14-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將將水質、溫度及老化後滲透與強度資料共同審查列為該構件的交接證據，連結到施工位置、材料批次及判讀版本。若發現材料溶出留下新通道，短期合格卻長期重新滲漏，先保留原始紀錄並由負責技師確認處置，不能以本課算例替代核定作業計畫。","textEn":"Apply the following check at handover: Review water chemistry, temperature and post-ageing permeability and strength together. Link results to location, material batch and interpretation version. If material leaching creates new pathways despite initially passing leakage checks, retain original records and obtain the responsible engineer's disposition; this example does not replace an approved work plan.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「水化學與耐久相容」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Water chemistry and durability compatibility\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","入口壓力升高就能證明整個處理區都已封閉","將水質、溫度及老化後滲透與強度資料共同審查。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Rising entrance pressure proves the entire treated zone is sealed","Review water chemistry, temperature and post-ageing permeability and strength together."],"answer":2,"explanation":"將水質、溫度及老化後滲透與強度資料共同審查。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Review water chemistry, temperature and post-ageing permeability and strength together. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b163-v14-36","title":"水化學與耐久相容：失效診斷","titleEn":"Water chemistry and durability compatibility: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b163-v14-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「水化學與耐久相容」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Water chemistry and durability compatibility” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"材料溶出留下新通道，短期合格卻長期重新滲漏。相似表徵也可能由量測偏差造成，因此應回到將水質、溫度及老化後滲透與強度資料共同審查，以獨立證據判別原因；只修補可見症狀將留下原本的傳力或滲流問題。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Material leaching creates new pathways despite initially passing leakage checks. Similar symptoms can arise from measurement bias: return to review water chemistry, temperature and post-ageing permeability and strength together to discriminate the cause. Treating visible symptoms alone leaves the original transfer or seepage problem unresolved. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：判別這個機制時，應觀察將水質、溫度及老化後滲透與強度資料共同審查；若出現材料溶出留下新通道，短期合格卻長期重新滲漏，便須重新檢查原先假設的接觸、力或水的傳遞邊界，而不能只調整計算結果。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: If material leaching creates new pathways despite initially passing leakage checks, revisit the assumed contact, force or water-transfer boundary rather than merely adjusting the calculated result.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「施工後短期不漏就代表材料永遠不會劣化」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Initial absence of leakage proves the material will never deteriorate\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b163-v14-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"材料溶出留下新通道，短期合格卻長期重新滲漏。相似表徵也可能由量測偏差造成，因此應回到將水質、溫度及老化後滲透與強度資料共同審查，以獨立證據判別原因；只修補可見症狀將留下原本的傳力或滲流問題。","textEn":"Material leaching creates new pathways despite initially passing leakage checks. Similar symptoms can arise from measurement bias: return to review water chemistry, temperature and post-ageing permeability and strength together to discriminate the cause. Treating visible symptoms alone leaves the original transfer or seepage problem unresolved.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"]},{"id":"b163-v14-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「水化學與耐久相容」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Water chemistry and durability compatibility\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["材料溶出留下新通道，短期合格卻長期重新滲漏。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","中心驗證孔合格就能代表整個止水範圍連續"],"optionsEn":["Material leaching creates new pathways despite initially passing leakage checks.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","A passing central verification hole proves the entire water barrier is continuous"],"answer":0,"explanation":"材料溶出留下新通道，短期合格卻長期重新滲漏。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Material leaching creates new pathways despite initially passing leakage checks. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b163-v14-37","title":"驗收範圍與長期水路：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Acceptance coverage and long-term pathways: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b163-v14-36"],"objective":"說明「驗收範圍與長期水路」如何影響高水壓隧道止水灌漿的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Acceptance coverage and long-term pathways” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Water-control grouting in high-pressure tunnels”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"止水效果需針對設計範圍與地下水邊界驗證，單孔低透水不能代表全部帷幕連續。水可能繞過未處理端部或沿新裂隙改道，交接應保存孔段、材料、量測水頭與未驗證區；維護才能分辨原缺口和後續變化。 判別這個機制時，應觀察將獨立驗證孔段與處理範圍及未驗證區逐一對照；若出現帷幕端部未封閉讓水繞流，中心孔合格仍無法控制湧水，便須重新檢查原先假設的接觸、力或水的傳遞邊界，而不能只調整計算結果。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「驗收範圍與長期水路」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Verify the design volume and groundwater boundary rather than treating low permeability in one hole as continuous coverage. Water can bypass ends or take new fractures. Preserve intervals, materials, test heads and unverified zones so maintenance distinguishes original gaps from later changes. Use the following check to discriminate the mechanism: Compare independent verification intervals with treatment extent and unverified zones. If an open treatment edge permits bypass despite passing central holes, revisit the assumed contact, force or water-transfer boundary rather than merely adjusting the calculated result. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Acceptance coverage and long-term pathways” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：verificationCoverage=verifiedIntervals/requiredIntervals=36/40=90 percent。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: verificationCoverage=verifiedIntervals/requiredIntervals=36/40=90 percent.","failure":"常見誤解：「中心驗證孔合格就能代表整個止水範圍連續」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A passing central verification hole proves the entire water barrier is continuous\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「驗收範圍與長期水路」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Acceptance coverage and long-term pathways”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b163-v14-37-k1","title":"驗收範圍與長期水路","titleEn":"Acceptance coverage and long-term pathways","text":"止水效果需針對設計範圍與地下水邊界驗證，單孔低透水不能代表全部帷幕連續。水可能繞過未處理端部或沿新裂隙改道，交接應保存孔段、材料、量測水頭與未驗證區；維護才能分辨原缺口和後續變化。","textEn":"Verify the design volume and groundwater boundary rather than treating low permeability in one hole as continuous coverage. Water can bypass ends or take new fractures.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"]},{"id":"b163-v14-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：中心驗證孔合格就能代表整個止水範圍連續 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A passing central verification hole proves the entire water barrier is continuous Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「驗收範圍與長期水路」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Acceptance coverage and long-term pathways\" is correct?","options":["中心驗證孔合格就能代表整個止水範圍連續","止水效果需針對設計範圍與地下水邊界驗證，單孔低透水不能代表全部帷幕連續。","隧道埋得多深就一定有完全相同的地下水頭"],"optionsEn":["A passing central verification hole proves the entire water barrier is continuous","Verify the design volume and groundwater boundary rather than treating low permeability in one hole as continuous coverage.","Tunnel burial depth always equals the groundwater head"],"answer":1,"explanation":"止水效果需針對設計範圍與地下水邊界驗證，單孔低透水不能代表全部帷幕連續。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Verify the design volume and groundwater boundary rather than treating low permeability in one hole as continuous coverage. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b163-v14-38","title":"驗收範圍與長期水路：定量估算","titleEn":"Acceptance coverage and long-term pathways: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b163-v14-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「驗收範圍與長期水路」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Acceptance coverage and long-term pathways” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：verificationCoverage=verifiedIntervals/requiredIntervals=36/40=90 percent。算例只描述水力關係，不提供現地配方、注入壓力或施作授權。 此結果僅用來核對量綱及模型敏感度，不是專案設計值、實測紀錄或現場允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: verificationCoverage=verifiedIntervals/requiredIntervals=36/40=90 percent. Examples describe hydraulic relationships, not field recipes, injection pressures or operating authorization. This checks dimensions and model sensitivity; it is neither measured project data nor a design or acceptance value. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將獨立驗證孔段與處理範圍及未驗證區逐一對照。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare independent verification intervals with treatment extent and unverified zones.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b163-v14-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：verificationCoverage=verifiedIntervals/requiredIntervals=36/40=90 percent。算例只描述水力關係，不提供現地配方、注入壓力或施作授權。 此結果僅用來核對量綱及模型敏感度，不是專案設計值、實測紀錄或現場允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: verificationCoverage=verifiedIntervals/requiredIntervals=36/40=90 percent. Examples describe hydraulic relationships, not field recipes, injection pressures or operating authorization. This checks dimensions and model sensitivity; it is neither measured project data nor a design or acceptance value.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"]},{"id":"b163-v14-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「驗收範圍與長期水路」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Acceptance coverage and long-term pathways\", which statement holds?","options":["淨注入壓差低就能保證任何地層都不會開裂","注入量達理論體積就能證明處理半徑完全達成","原創教學假設：verificationCoverage=verifiedIntervals/requiredIntervals=36/40=90 percent。"],"optionsEn":["A low net injection difference guarantees no ground can fracture","Delivered theoretical volume proves the complete treatment radius has been achieved","Original teaching assumptions: verificationCoverage=verifiedIntervals/requiredIntervals=36/40=90 percent."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：verificationCoverage=verifiedIntervals/requiredIntervals=36/40=90 percent。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: verificationCoverage=verifiedIntervals/requiredIntervals=36/40=90 percent. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b163-v14-39","title":"驗收範圍與長期水路：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Acceptance coverage and long-term pathways: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b163-v14-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「驗收範圍與長期水路」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Acceptance coverage and long-term pathways” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將獨立驗證孔段與處理範圍及未驗證區逐一對照。量測須保存位置、時間及基準，讓同條件的重複結果可比較；並特別檢查「帷幕端部未封閉讓水繞流，中心孔合格仍無法控制湧水」是否能由這組資料區分。儀器校核與誤差估計應先於判讀，由負責技師核定該項試驗的允收和停留點。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare independent verification intervals with treatment extent and unverified zones. Retain position, time and datums for comparable repeats, specifically distinguishing this scenario: An open treatment edge permits bypass despite passing central holes. Instrument checks and uncertainty estimates precede interpretation; the responsible engineer sets acceptance and hold points for this test. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將將獨立驗證孔段與處理範圍及未驗證區逐一對照列為該構件的交接證據，連結到施工位置、材料批次及判讀版本。若發現帷幕端部未封閉讓水繞流，中心孔合格仍無法控制湧水，先保留原始紀錄並由負責技師確認處置，不能以本課算例替代核定作業計畫。","observationEn":"Site practice: Apply the following check at handover: Compare independent verification intervals with treatment extent and unverified zones. Link results to location, material batch and interpretation version. If an open treatment edge permits bypass despite passing central holes, retain original records and obtain the responsible engineer's disposition; this example does not replace an approved work plan.","failure":"注意干擾：帷幕端部未封閉讓水繞流，中心孔合格仍無法控制湧水。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: An open treatment edge permits bypass despite passing central holes. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b163-v14-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將獨立驗證孔段與處理範圍及未驗證區逐一對照。量測須保存位置、時間及基準，讓同條件的重複結果可比較；並特別檢查「帷幕端部未封閉讓水繞流，中心孔合格仍無法控制湧水」是否能由這組資料區分。儀器校核與誤差估計應先於判讀，由負責技師核定該項試驗的允收和停留點。","textEn":"Compare independent verification intervals with treatment extent and unverified zones. Retain position, time and datums for comparable repeats, specifically distinguishing this scenario: An open treatment edge permits bypass despite passing central holes. Instrument checks and uncertainty estimates precede interpretation; the responsible engineer sets acceptance and hold points for this test.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"]},{"id":"b163-v14-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將將獨立驗證孔段與處理範圍及未驗證區逐一對照列為該構件的交接證據，連結到施工位置、材料批次及判讀版本。若發現帷幕端部未封閉讓水繞流，中心孔合格仍無法控制湧水，先保留原始紀錄並由負責技師確認處置，不能以本課算例替代核定作業計畫。","textEn":"Apply the following check at handover: Compare independent verification intervals with treatment extent and unverified zones. Link results to location, material batch and interpretation version. If an open treatment edge permits bypass despite passing central holes, retain original records and obtain the responsible engineer's disposition; this example does not replace an approved work plan.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「驗收範圍與長期水路」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Acceptance coverage and long-term pathways\"?","options":["將獨立驗證孔段與處理範圍及未驗證區逐一對照。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","處理後流量降低就一定全部來自灌漿改善"],"optionsEn":["Compare independent verification intervals with treatment extent and unverified zones.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Every post-treatment flow decrease is entirely caused by grouting improvement"],"answer":0,"explanation":"將獨立驗證孔段與處理範圍及未驗證區逐一對照。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare independent verification intervals with treatment extent and unverified zones. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b163-v14-40","title":"驗收範圍與長期水路：失效診斷","titleEn":"Acceptance coverage and long-term pathways: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b163-v14-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「驗收範圍與長期水路」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Acceptance coverage and long-term pathways” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"帷幕端部未封閉讓水繞流，中心孔合格仍無法控制湧水。相似表徵也可能由量測偏差造成，因此應回到將獨立驗證孔段與處理範圍及未驗證區逐一對照，以獨立證據判別原因；只修補可見症狀將留下原本的傳力或滲流問題。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"An open treatment edge permits bypass despite passing central holes. Similar symptoms can arise from measurement bias: return to compare independent verification intervals with treatment extent and unverified zones to discriminate the cause. Treating visible symptoms alone leaves the original transfer or seepage problem unresolved. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：判別這個機制時，應觀察將獨立驗證孔段與處理範圍及未驗證區逐一對照；若出現帷幕端部未封閉讓水繞流，中心孔合格仍無法控制湧水，便須重新檢查原先假設的接觸、力或水的傳遞邊界，而不能只調整計算結果。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: If an open treatment edge permits bypass despite passing central holes, revisit the assumed contact, force or water-transfer boundary rather than merely adjusting the calculated result.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「中心驗證孔合格就能代表整個止水範圍連續」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A passing central verification hole proves the entire water barrier is continuous\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b163-v14-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"帷幕端部未封閉讓水繞流，中心孔合格仍無法控制湧水。相似表徵也可能由量測偏差造成，因此應回到將獨立驗證孔段與處理範圍及未驗證區逐一對照，以獨立證據判別原因；只修補可見症狀將留下原本的傳力或滲流問題。","textEn":"An open treatment edge permits bypass despite passing central holes. Similar symptoms can arise from measurement bias: return to compare independent verification intervals with treatment extent and unverified zones to discriminate the cause. Treating visible symptoms alone leaves the original transfer or seepage problem unresolved.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"]},{"id":"b163-v14-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「驗收範圍與長期水路」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Acceptance coverage and long-term pathways\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","帷幕端部未封閉讓水繞流，中心孔合格仍無法控制湧水。","隧道埋得多深就一定有完全相同的地下水頭"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","An open treatment edge permits bypass despite passing central holes.","Tunnel burial depth always equals the groundwater head"],"answer":1,"explanation":"帷幕端部未封閉讓水繞流，中心孔合格仍無法控制湧水。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"An open treatment edge permits bypass despite passing central holes. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-fhwa-tomie","v14s-sika-tunnel"],"curriculumVersion":14,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000}};
